\v 7 \add #Pigs\add* have divided¦50889 \add #hooves¦50890\add* that are split completely, \add ≈but¦50884\add* don't¦50897 \add ≈chew\add* the¦50886 cud¦50896, \add so\add* they're ‘unclean¦50900’ for you all—
\v 8 you mustn't eat¦50906 their meat¦50904 or touch¦50909 their carcasses¦50907 \add because\add* they're ‘unclean¦50910’ for you all.
\p
\v 9 ⇔You all can eat¦50931 everything that¦50916 \add lives\add* in¦50929 the water¦50927, \add whether\add* the oceans or rivers, as long as it has \add both\add* fins and scales¦50926.
\v 10 \add ≈In contrast,\add* anything in the oceans or rivers without \add both\add* fins and¦50933 scales¦50939, whether they're swarming¦50943 creatures¦50946 or otherwise, they'll \add all\add* be detestable¦50950 for you all.
\v 11 \add ≈So¦50954\add* anything that's detestable¦50954 to¦50956 you all, you mustn't eat¦50959 their meat¦50957 and¦50954 you must¦50955 detest¦50954 their carcasses¦50962.
\v 12 Anything in the water¦50972 that doesn't have \add both\add* fins and¦50971 scales¦50971 will be detestable¦50973 for you all.
\p
\v 13 From¦50981 the birds, the ones that you'll all detest¦50980 and avoid eating¦50985 will¦50986 include: the eagle¦50990 and \add ≈any kind of\add* vulture¦50995,
