\v 16 \add ≈any kind¦51023 of¦51012\add* owl¦51016, gull¦51019, or hawk,
\v 17 the cormorant¦51030,
\v 18 the osprey,
\v 19 the stork¦51046, any kind¦51048 of heron¦51047, the hoopoe¦51051, and¦51045 bats.
\v 20 Everything¦51056 that¦51059 swarms¦51057 with wings and walks¦51059 on¦51060 four¦51062 \add legs\add* must be detestable¦51063 for you all.
\v 21 However, you all¦51073 can eat¦51072 anything that swarms¦51074 with wings and walks¦51076 on four¦51079 \add legs\add* that has its legs above¦51085 its feet¦51086 for hopping on the¦51091 ground.
\v 22 You all can eat¦51097 any kind of locust or cricket or grasshopper¦51112,
\v 23 \add ≈but¦51115\add* anything that¦51118 swarms¦51116 with wings and¦51115 walks on four¦51121 \add legs\add* must be detestable¦51123 for you all¦51115.
\rem /s1 Unclean Animals
\p
\v 24 \add ≈The following\add* will make¦51128 you¦51128 ‘unclean’—anyone¦51131 who¦51131 touches¦51131 their¦51132 carcasses¦51132 will become ‘unclean’ until¦51134 the¦51136 evening¦51136,
\v 25 plus¦51144 anyone¦51140 who¦51140 carries¦51140 their carcass¦51141 must¦51142 wash¦51142 their clothes¦51143 and¦51138 will be¦51144 ‘unclean¦51144’ until¦51145 the¦51147 evening¦51147:
\v 26 Any¦51149 animal with a divided¦51154 hoof¦51155 but¦51156 not \add ≈completely split in two¦51154\add* or that¦51152 doesn't \add ≈chew\add* the cud¦51160 will be¦51170 ‘unclean’ for¦51165 you all—anyone¦51168 who¦51168 touches¦51168 them¦51169 will become ‘unclean’.
\v 27 \add ≈Also¦51172,\add* any¦51172 four-footed animal that¦51174 walks¦51174 on¦51175 its¦51177 paws¦51177 is ‘unclean’ for¦51187 you—anyone¦51174 who¦51190 touches¦51190 their¦51191 carcass¦51191 will¦51192 become ‘unclean’ until¦51193 the¦51195 evening¦51195,
\v 28 plus¦51203 anyone¦51197 who¦51197 carries¦51197 their carcass¦51200 must¦51201 wash¦51201 their clothes¦51202 and¦51197 will¦51207 be¦51203 ‘unclean’ until¦51204 the¦51206 evening¦51206 \add because\add* they're ‘unclean’ for you all.
\p
\v 29 These are the ‘unclean¦51214’ creatures from the ones that¦51216 swarm¦51216 on the ground: \add #rats, mice, lizards¦51222\add*
\v 30 of any kind, \add #geckos¦51225, skinks¦51228, and¦51225 chameleons¦51229\add*.
\v 31 Out of all the swarming¦51236 things¦51236, those are ‘unclean’ for¦51233 you—anyone¦51239 who¦51239 touches¦51239 them¦51240 when they've died will¦51242 be¦51242 ‘unclean’ until¦51243 the evening¦51245.
\v 32 \add ≈Also¦51247,\add* anything that¦51272 \add ≈their¦51255 dead bodies\add* fall¦51250 on¦51252 will become ‘unclean’, whether it's a wooden. cloth, leader, or sackcloth¦51268 object, or any container used for work¦51275, \add so then\add* it must¦51250 be immersed in water¦51277 and¦51247 it will be ‘unclean’ until¦51280 the¦51282 evening¦51282 when it will become ‘clean’ \add again\add*.
\v 33 \add If\add* one of¦51287 \add @those creatures\add* falls¦51292 into¦51294 a clay container, everything in¦51299 it will become ‘unclean¦51300’ and¦51285 you must¦51292 break¦51302 \add @that¦51290 container\add*.
\v 34 If water¦51312 from \add that container\add* got onto any food¦51306, it will become ‘unclean’, and¦51314 any drink¦51316 \add ≈take\add* from that container will be¦51322 ‘unclean’.
\v 35 Anything that¦51325 the dead body of one of \add @those creatures\add* falls¦51327 onto will¦51331 become ‘unclean’—any oven¦51332 or stove¦51333 must¦51327 be¦51334 smashed. They¦51336 have become ‘unclean’ \add ≈and¦51324 would always remain so\add*.
\v 36 However a spring¦51342 or a cistern¦51343 for collecting¦51344 water¦51346 will be ‘clean’, \add ≈but¦51343\add* anyone¦51349 touching¦51349 that dead body will be ‘unclean¦51351’.
\v 37 If the dead body fell¦51354 on¦51356 some seeds that will¦51363 be¦51363 planted, \add @that seed¦51360\add* is¦51364 still ‘clean’,
\v 38 \add ≈but¦51367\add* if the seeds \add ≈are wet\add* when¦51367 the dead body falls¦51374 on it, then¦51367 it's ‘unclean¦51377’ for you.
\p
\v 39 If any animal that¦51387 you all can eat dies¦51383, then any person touches¦51392 its¦51393 carcass¦51393 will¦51394 be¦51394 ‘unclean¦51394’ until¦51395 the¦51397 evening¦51397.
\v 40 Anyone¦51399 who eats¦51399 any¦51400 \add part\add* of that dead body, and anyone¦51399 who \add ≈moves\add* it, must¦51401 wash¦51411 their clothes¦51402 and will¦51413 be¦51413 ‘unclean¦51413’ until¦51414 the¦51416 evening¦51416.
\p
\v 41 Every creature that¦51421 swarms¦51420 along the ground is¦51425 detestable¦51425—it mustn't be¦51428 eaten¦51428.
\v 42 Everything that \add moves\add* on its belly, and¦51436 any swarming thing that moves along the ground on four¦51441 or more feet mustn't be eaten because¦51456 they're detestable.
\v 43 Don't¦51461 make yourselves detestable¦51463 with any of those swarming¦51469 creatures, and don't¦51461 make yourselves ‘unclean¦51474’ by¦51475 \add touching or eating\add* them¦51475,
\v 44 because I am¦51479 your god¦51480 Yahweh¦51479. You¦51481 all must¦51481 keep¦51481 yourselves holy, and¦51482 you're a holy people because I'm¦51478 holy. \add ≈So\add* don't¦51487 make¦51488 yourselves ‘unclean¦51488’ with any swarming¦51494 creatures that creep¦51495 across the ground\x + \xo 11:44: \xt Lev 19:2; 1Pe 1:16.\x*
\v 45 because I am Yahweh¦51503, the one who brought¦51504 you all out of¦51506 Egypt¦51507 to be your god¦51510, and¦51511 you must¦51511 be holy because I am holy.
\p
\v 46 The \add above\add* are the regulations about¦51518 livestock¦51519, birds, creatures that move in the water¦51525, and¦51526 creatures that swarm¦51529 across the ground,
\v 47 to \add ≈distinguish\add* between¦51535 the ‘unclean¦51536’ and the ‘clean’, i.e., those that can be eaten and those that must¦51546 not¦51545 be eaten.
\c 12
\s1 Purification after giving birth
\rem /s1 The Purification of Women after Childbirth; Purification after Childbirth; Purification of Women after Childbirth; Purification After Childbirth
\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦51550 told¦51554 Mosheh¦51553:
\p
\v 2 Tell¦51560 the¦51559 \add ≈Israelis¦51559\add* that when a woman¦51562 gets pregnant and then gives birth to a boy, she will then be¦51567 ‘unclean’ for seven¦51568 days similar to how her impurity¦51571 during her \add ≈monthly period\add* makes her ‘unclean’.
\v 3 Then¦51575 on¦51575 the eighth¦51576 day¦51575, \add @the baby boy's\add* foreskin¦51579 must¦51577 be¦51577 circumcised¦51577.\x + \xo 12:3: \xt Gen 17:12; Luk 2:21.\x*
\v 4 \add @The mother\add* will¦51601 remain¦51585 impure from the blood¦51586 for thirty-three¦51581 days¦51582—she must¦51585 not touch¦51593 any sacred¦51590 thing¦51590 and¦51581 may not enter the sanctuary¦51596 until¦51599 her¦51602 purification¦51587 time¦51584 is completed¦51601.
\p
\v 5 \add ≈However,\add* if¦51605 she gave birth to a \add ≈girl\add*, she'll¦51608 be ‘unclean¦51609’ for two¦51610 weeks¦51610 similar to how her impurity¦51611 during her \add ≈monthly period\add*, and¦51605 her purification¦51620 time¦51615 will¦51616 be sixty-six¦51612 days¦51615.
\p
\v 6 When¦51622 \add @the mother's\add* purification¦51625 time¦51624 is completed¦51622 for¦51626 either a son¦51626 or a daughter¦51628, she¦51629 must¦51629 take a one-year-old lamb¦51630 as a burnt¦51634 offering and¦51622 a \add ≈young¦51635\add* pigeon or dove¦51637 as a sin¦51641 offering to the priest¦51650 at the entrance¦51644 to the \add ≈sacred¦51645\add* tent¦51645.
\v 7 Then¦51652 he¦51652 must¦51652 present¦51652 them to Yahweh¦51654 to \add ≈make¦51655 her right with God\add*, and¦51652 then¦51652 she'll¦51657 be¦51657 purified from¦51658 her flow of blood¦51659. That's the regulation for a woman who gives¦51662 birth¦51662 to either a male¦51663 or¦51664 a female¦51665.
\p
\v 8 If¦51667 \add ≈she's unable to afford\add* a lamb, then she must¦51670 take¦51674 \em two\em* young¦51680 pigeons or¦51678 doves—one for the burnt¦51683 offering and one for the sin¦51685 offering. Then¦51667 the priest¦51688 will \add ≈make¦51686 her¦51671 right with God\add*, and then she'll¦51674 will have been purified.\x + \xo 12:8: \xt Luk 2:24.\x*
\c 13
\s1 Regulations about skin diseases
\rem /s1 Laws concerning Skin Diseases; Contagious Skin Diseases; Leprosy, Varieties and Symptoms; Regulations About Infectious Skin Diseases
\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦51693 told Mosheh¦51696 and¦51697 Aharon¦51699:
\p
\v 2 If¦51703 \add someone discovers\add* a raised area on¦51706 their skin, or a scab or a bright¦51714 spot¦51714, and¦51715 it¦51715 seems like an infectious skin disease¦51720, then \add @that person\add* should be¦51721 taken to¦51722 a priest¦51725 (Aharon¦51724 or one¦51729 of his¦51730 sons¦51730),
\v 3 and the priest must \add ≈examine\add* their skin. If the hair¦51741 in the infected \add spot\add* has¦51743 turned¦51743 white¦51745 and the infection appears¦51746 to be deeper under the skin, then¦51733 it's \add confirmed as\add* an infectious skin disease¦51752 and \add ≈so\add* the priest must pronounce the person as ‘unclean¦51756’.
\v 4 \add However,\add* if¦51759 it's a white spot \add ≈that doesn't seem\add* to be deep¦51766, and¦51759 the hair¦51773 hasn't turned¦51776 white, then¦51759 the priest¦51779 \add must order\add* the person to be quarantined for seven¦51783 days¦51784.
\v 5 Then¦51786 on the seventh¦51789 day¦51788, if the infection is still there but¦51786 hasn't spread¦51796, then¦51786 the priest¦51787 \add must order\add* a further seven¦51801 days¦51802 of quarantine.
\v 6 After¦51811 that next seven¦51809 days, if the infection has¦51812 faded and not¦51814 spread¦51816, the priest¦51806 must pronounce the person as ‘clean’—it was just a \add ≈sore\add* so the person must wash¦51823 their clothes¦51824 and then¦51805 they'll be¦51825 ‘clean’.
\v 7 \add ≈However,\add* if¦51827 the spot does spread across the skin \em after¦51833\em* the priest has¦51834 pronounced \add @the person\add* to be ‘clean’, then¦51827 they must¦51830 \add ≈return\add* to the priest a second¦51840 time.
\v 8 The¦51847 priest must re-examine \add @that person\add* and¦51845 if the spot on the skin has¦51848 spread¦51848, then¦51845 the priest must pronounce them ‘unclean¦51851’ because they have a skin disease¦51853.
\p
\v 9 Anyone¦51861 who develops an infectious skin¦51858 disease¦51858 must¦51860 be¦51862 taken to¦51863 a priest¦51865
\v 10 \add ≈to be examined\add*. If¦51869 it's a white spot on the skin¦51873 and the hair¦51876 has¦51875 turned¦51875 white, and there's raw¦51878 flesh¦51879 \add visible\add* in¦51881 the swelling¦51881,
\v 11 then it's¦51885 a chronic skin¦51886 disease¦51883, and the¦51889 priest¦51889 must¦51888 pronounce \add @that person\add* as ‘unclean¦51893’ and can't¦51890 just be \add temporarily\add* \add ≈quarantined\add*.
\v 12 \add ≈However,\add* if¦51896 the disease has broken out and¦51896 spread across the entire¦51905 \add ≈body\add* from¦51909 head¦51909 to¦51913 toe as far as can be observed by the priest¦51917,
\v 13 then¦51919 \add after\add* the priest's¦51920 confirmation that it covers¦51922 the entire¦51926 \add ≈body¦51928\add*, \add @that person\add* can be pronounced as ‘clean’ \add again\add* as all¦51926 of it has¦51934 turned¦51934 white¦51935.
\v 14 \add ≈However,\add* if any raw flesh¦51942 \add ≈shows itself\add*, then¦51939 they'll become ‘unclean¦51944’ \add ≈that same\add* day¦51939.
\v 15 The priest¦51947 must \add ≈examine\add* that raw flesh and¦51952 must pronounce \add @that person\add* as ‘unclean’ due to \add &their\add* skin¦51957 disease¦51957.
\v 16 \add ≈Afterwards, if¦51961 it heals over\add* and goes¦51967 white¦51966, then they can return¦51962 to the¦51970 priest¦51970
\v 17 \add ≈to be reexamined\add*, and if the infection has¦51975 indeed gone white¦51977, then¦51972 the priest¦51973 can pronounce it as \add ≈not being infectious\add* and \add @the person\add* as ‘clean’ \add again\add*.
\p
\v 18 When \add ≈someone\add* has a boil¦51994 on¦51993 their skin¦51993, \add ≈but¦51987\add* it¦51995 heals¦51995
\v 19 \add ≈leaving behind\add* a white swelling¦52000 or¦52002 a reddish-white¦52005 bright¦52003 spot¦52003, then¦51997 \add @that person\add* must¦52006 show themself to¦52007 the¦52009 priest¦52009.
\v 20 The¦52013 priest will \add ≈examine\add* it, and if it is¦52015 indeed more¦52016 than¦52016 \add just\add* skin deep and its¦52019 hair¦52019 has turned¦52020 white¦52021, then¦52011 the priest must¦52011 pronounce \add @that person\add* as ‘unclean¦52022’ because an infectious skin disease¦52026 has broken¦52029 out¦52029 from the \add original\add* boil¦52028.
\v 21 \add ≈However¦52035,\add* if¦52031 the¦52034 priest's¦52034 examination finds not white¦52040 hair¦52039 on it, and it's not more¦52043 than¦52043 skin¦52045 deep¦52041, and it's fading, then¦52031 he¦52048 will¦52048 \add order\add* \add @that person\add* quarantined for seven¦52050 days¦52051,
\v 22 and¦52053 if¦52053 it spreads¦52056 further on \add &their\add* skin¦52057, then¦52053 the¦52059 priest¦52059 must¦52056 declare¦52058 \add @that person\add* as ‘unclean¦52058’ because it's \add ≈infectious\add*.
\v 23 \add ≈But¦52064\add* if¦52064 the bright¦52068 spot¦52068 \add ≈hasn't spread¦52070\add* \add during the quarantine\add*, then¦52064 it's \add just\add* the scar¦52071 from the boil¦52072 and¦52074 the priest¦52075 can pronounce \add @the person\add* as ‘clean’.
\p
\v 24 If¦52080 someone gets a burn on¦52083 their skin¦52083, and¦52087 the burn area becomes reddish-white¦52092 or¦52093 a white spot,
\v 25 then the priest must examine it, and if the hair¦52101 on the spot¦52103 has turned¦52100 white¦52102 and \add @the infection\add* looks more¦52106 than¦52106 skin deep, then a skin disease¦52109 has broken¦52112 out¦52112 in the burn¦52111, and the priest must pronounce \add @that person\add* as ‘unclean¦52113’ because it's¦52118 \add ≈infectious\add*.
\v 26 \add ≈However¦52124,\add* if¦52120 the priest¦52123 sees¦52122 that there's¦52125 no white¦52129 hair¦52128 in¦52127 the spot¦52127, and it's not more¦52132 than¦52132 skin¦52134 deep¦52130, and it's fading, then¦52120 \add *he¦52137\add* will¦52137 \add order\add* \add @that person\add* quarantined for seven¦52139 days¦52140.
\v 27 On the seventh¦52145 day¦52144, the priest¦52143 will re-examine \add @the person\add*, and¦52151 if¦52146 it's spread¦52149 further, \add *he¦52151\add* must¦52142 pronounce \add @that person\add* as ‘unclean¦52151’ because it's an infectious skin¦52155 disease¦52155.
\v 28 \add ≈But¦52158\add* if¦52158 the bright¦52162 spot¦52162 hasn't spread¦52165 on the skin¦52166, and¦52158 it faded \add more\add*, then¦52158 it was \add just\add* swelling¦52169 from the burn. Then¦52158 the priest¦52173 will pronounce \add @that person\add* to be ‘clean’ because¦52174 it was \add just\add* the scar¦52176 \add ≈caused by\add* \add &their\add* burn.
\p
\v 29 If a man¦52181 or woman¦52183 has an infection in \add &their\add* \add ≈scalp\add* or \add ≈under\add* \add &their\add* beard¦52191,
\v 30 then the priest should inspect the infection. If¦52198 it appears¦52199 to be more¦52201 than¦52201 skin deep, and there's any thin¦52207 yellow¦52206 hairs in¦52204 it, then the priest must¦52193 pronounce \add @that person\add* as ‘unclean¦52208’ \add because\add* it's¦52212 a \add ≈itchy and infectious\add* skin infection on the \add ≈scalp or¦52215 face\add*.
\v 31 \add ≈However¦52227,\add* if the priest¦52222 notices an itchy infection yet it's only skin deep and¦52219 there's¦52237 no black¦52236 hair¦52235 on¦52238 it, then¦52219 he¦52239 should quarantine that person for seven¦52245 days¦52246.
\v 32 On¦52255 the seventh¦52254 day¦52253, the priest¦52249 will re-examine \add ≈that person\add* and if the spot hasn't widened and \add still\add* only appears¦52266 to be skin deep,
\v 33 then \add @that person\add* should shave \add their head\add*, and¦52274 then the priest¦52281 should quarantine them for a further seven¦52285 days¦52286.
\v 34 Then¦52289 \add again\add* on the seventh¦52295 day¦52294, the priest will inspect it, and if the spot hasn't widened after being shaved and it doesn't seem to be more¦52305 than¦52305 skin¦52301 deep¦52304, then¦52289 the priest can pronounce \add @that person\add* as ‘clean’ \add ≈once\add* they've washed¦52311 their clothes¦52312.
\v 35 \add ≈However,\add* it¦52318 is did spread on their skin¦52320 after¦52321 \add *that\add*,
\v 36 then the priest¦52325 must¦52324 inspect it again, and¦52324 if it's spread¦52327 then \add @that person\add* is ‘unclean¦52336’ (whether or not there's any yellow¦52335 hair¦52334).
\v 37 \add ≈But¦52339\add* if¦52339 it seems that the spot \add ≈hasn't spread\add* and dark hair¦52344 is growing in¦52348 it again, then¦52339 \add @that person's\add* \add ≈not infectious\add* and the priest¦52354 can pronounce them as ‘clean’.
\p
\v 38 If¦52361 a man¦52357 or¦52358 woman¦52360 \add ≈finds very\add* white¦52369 spots on¦52364 their¦52366 skin¦52364,
\v 39 then the priest¦52372 must¦52371 examine \add <them\add*. If¦52373 the spots¦52377 on their¦52376 skin are dull¦52378 white¦52379, then it's a skin rash¦52380 that's broken¦52382 out and¦52373 they are ‘clean’.
\p
\v 40 If¦52389 a man's head¦52391 has become¦52390 bare¦52390, then he's¦52393 \add gone\add* bald¦52392 and¦52388 is¦52394 \add still\add* ‘clean’.
\v 41 \add ≈Similarly,\add* if¦52397 the hair \add ≈is receding\add* from the front corners, he's¦52403 \add ≈going bald¦52402\add* and¦52397 is \add still\add* ‘clean’.
\v 42 \add ≈However,\add* if there's a balding spot with a reddish-white¦52415 infection, it's a skin¦52416 disease¦52416 breaking¦52417 out via that¦52417 spot
\v 43 and¦52426 the priest¦52425 must¦52423 examine him¦52424. If¦52426 it's¦52424 a balding spot¦52432 with a reddish-white¦52431 infection that looks like¦52435 a \add contagious\add* skin disease¦52436,
\v 44 then he's¦52443 \add ≈contagious\add* and ‘unclean’. The¦52448 priest¦52448 must¦52447 pronounce his as ‘unclean’ because of¦52450 that infection on¦52449 his head¦52449.
\p
\v 45 Anyone¦52452 who's¦52452 developed an infectious skin¦52452 disease¦52452 must tear¦52459 their clothes¦52457 and \add ≈leave their hair loose\add*, and must \add ≈cover¦52466 their mouth\add* and call¦52470 out¦52470, ‘Unclean¦52467, unclean¦52469.’
\v 46 They will¦52478 remain ‘unclean’ as long as they \add still\add* have that¦52475 infection, and must¦52478 live alone¦52481 outside¦52483 the¦52483 camp¦52484.
\s1 Regulations about moulds and fungi
\rem /s1 Laws concerning Mildew; Regulations About Mildew; Treatment of Contaminated Clothing
\p
\v 47 When a \add piece of\add* clothing¦52488 has a mould growing on it, whether it's¦52492 made of wool¦52496 or¦52497 linen¦52499,
\v 48 or whether it's something woven from wool¦52506 or linen¦52505, or something made from leather,
\v 49 if the growth is greenish¦52517 or¦52519 reddish¦52520 in colour, then¦52515 it's¦52538 something that can spread and¦52515 it must¦52539 be¦52539 shown¦52539 to¦52539 the priest¦52542.
\v 50 The¦52545 priest¦52545 must¦52544 examine the growth, and¦52549 quarantine the \add ≈article\add* for seven¦52553 days¦52554.
\v 51 On the seventh¦52561 day¦52560, if¦52562 the growth has¦52564 spread¦52564 on that piece of material or leather equipment, and it's¦52578 confirmed as spreadable and is ‘unclean¦52584’.
\v 52 \add ?@The owner\add* must burn¦52587 the piece of clothing or equipment that¦52610 contains the infection because¦52615 it's contagious, so it must be¦52621 completely burnt¦52621 up.
\p
\v 53 \add ≈However¦52626\add* if¦52623 the priest¦52625 notices that the growth hasn't spread¦52629 on the clothing or on the woven or leather \add ≈material\add*,
\v 54 then the priest¦52644 must¦52643 order that¦52647 the \add ≈material\add* be washed¦52645 and¦52643 then quarantined for a \add ≈further\add* seven¦52652 days¦52654.
\v 55 \add On the seventh day,\add* the priest¦52658 must inspect that washed¦52661 \add ≈material\add*, and if the growth hasn't \add ≈changed its¦52672 appearance\add*, even if it hasn't spread¦52676, then¦52657 it's ‘unclean¦52677’ and must be burnt¦52680 in the fire¦52679—it's a mildew¦52681 that's on¦52683 the front¦52685 or¦52684 back of¦52685 the material.
\v 56 \add ≈However¦52690,\add* if¦52687 the priest¦52689 notices that the growth has faded after¦52693 being washed¦52694, then¦52687 it can be torn¦52696 out of the clothing¦52700 or piece of leather or woven material.
\v 57 If¦52714 it \add then\add* reappears on that clothing or material, then it's breaking¦52731 out, so then that article¦52728 must¦52716 be burnt¦52734 in¦52738 the¦52739 fire¦52733.
\v 58 \add ≈On the other hand,\add* if the growth \add ≈vanished after being\add* washed, then it must¦52755 be washed a second¦52760 time and¦52741 then it will¦52761 be ‘clean’.
\p
\v 59 \add @The above\add* are the regulations concerning any growth on a piece of woollen or linen¦52772 clothing¦52768 or fabric, or any leather article¦52780, to¦52783 pronounce it¦52783 ‘clean’ or ‘unclean¦52785’.
\c 14
\s1 Purification after a skin disease
\rem /s1 Purification after Having Skin Diseases; Cleansing from Skin Diseases; Purification of Lepers and Leprous Houses; Cleansing From Infectious Skin Diseases
\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦52789 told¦52793 Mosheh¦52792:
\p
\v 2 These are the regulations for the purification¦52800 of a person who had¦52798 a skin¦52798 disease¦52798. They must¦52796 be¦52801 taken to¦52802 a priest¦52804\x + \xo 14:2: \xt Mat 8:4; Mrk 1:44; Luk 5:14; 17:14.\x*
\v 3 \add *who'll\add* go¦52806 outside¦52810 the camp¦52811 \add to meet them\add*. The¦52814 priest¦52807 must¦52806 inspect \add that person\add*, and¦52806 if the skin disease has¦52815 indeed left them,
\v 4 then¦52823 the¦52824 priest¦52824 will¦52825 order them to bring \add <him\add* two¦52827 live¦52830, ‘clean’ birds¦52829, some cedar¦52833 \add wood\add*, some scarlet¦52834 \add thread\add*, and¦52823 some hyssop¦52836 \add twigs\add*.
\v 5 The priest¦52839 must¦52838 tell \add @the person\add* to slaughter one bird¦52843 \add ?≈so the blood runs into¦52845\add* a clay jug \add ?≈containing\add* water¦52852 \add ≈from a spring or creek\add*.
\v 6 Then \add @the priest\add* will¦52859 take¦52859 the live bird, along with the cedar¦52864 wood¦52863, the scarlet¦52867 \add thread\add*, and the hyssop¦52871 \add twigs\add*, and dip¦52872 them¦52873 \add ≈all\add* into that¦52880 blood¦52878 of¦52878 the slaughtered bird (\add ?≈mixed with\add* the \add ≈fresh\add* water¦52882),
\v 7 and \add ≈flick\add* it seven¦52891 times¦52892 onto the person who's being purified¦52887 from¦52888 the skin¦52890 disease¦52890. Then¦52885 \add @the priest\add* can pronounce them as ‘clean’ \add enough to re-enter the community\add*, and \add ≈release\add* the live¦52898 bird¦52897 \add to fly\add* into the countryside¦52902.
\v 8 The person who's being purified¦52905 must then wash their clothes¦52908, shave¦52909 all their hair¦52914, and¦52904 then bathe in \add flowing\add* water¦52916. After¦52918 that, they can re-enter the camp¦52922 \add ≈but¦52904\add* must live outside¦52924 their tent¦52925 for seven¦52926 \add more\add* days¦52927.
\v 9 On¦52930 the seventh¦52931 day¦52930, \add @that person\add* must¦52932 shave¦52932 off all their hair (including¦52941 eyebrows¦52945 and beard¦52943 \add if appropriate\add*), wash their clothes¦52956 and bathe themself in \add flowing\add* water¦52961, then¦52929 they'll be¦52962 ‘clean’.
\p
\v 10 Then¦52964 on¦52964 the¦52965 eighth¦52965 day¦52964, \add @that person\add* must¦52966 \add ≈get\add* two¦52967 one-year-old \add male\add* lambs¦52969, and¦52964 one female lamb, \add all\add* \add ≈with no defects\add*, along with three¦52977 kilograms of fine¦52979 flour¦52979 mixed¦52981 with oil as a grain¦52980 offering¦52980, as well as \add ≈half a litre\add* of \add olive\add* oil.
\v 11 \add That must be taken to\add* the priest¦52988 who'd pronounced them as ‘clean’ \add ≈will accompany them\add* and¦52993 all those offerings to stand \add ≈in¦52994 front¦52994\add* of¦52994 Yahweh¦52995 at the entrance¦52996 to the \add ≈sacred¦52997\add* tent¦52997.
\v 12 Then¦53000 the priest¦53001 must¦53000 take¦53000 one of the male¦53004 lambs and the \add ≈container\add* of oil¦53012 and present¦53006 it as a guilt¦53008 offering, then¦53000 he'll¦53006 raise them as a wave¦53013 offering \add ≈in¦53016 front¦53016\add* of Yahweh¦53017.
\v 13 Then¦53019 \add @that person\add* must¦53019 slaughter that lamb¦53022 in the sacred place¦53023 where¦53024 sin offerings and¦53019 burnt¦53031 offerings are slaughtered, because¦53034 this guilt¦53036 offering is like¦53035 a sin offering in that it's for the priest¦53038—it's \add ≈very\add* sacred.
\v 14 Then¦53043 the priest¦53044 must¦53043 take¦53043 some¦53045 of the blood¦53045 from that guilt¦53046 offering¦53046, and put it¦53047 on the lobe¦53051 of the right ear¦53052 of the person being purified¦53053, and on their right thumb¦53057 and right big¦53062 toe¦53062.
\v 15 Then¦53066 the priest¦53067 must¦53066 take¦53066 \add ≈the container\add* of¦53073 olive oil¦53069 and¦53070 pour¦53070 some into his left¦53075 hand.
\v 16 Then¦53077 he'll¦53077 dip¦53077 his right¦53082 finger into that oil¦53085 on¦53087 his left¦53090 palm¦53089, and¦53077 with¦53095 that \add same\add* finger, \add ≈flick\add* it seven¦53096 times¦53097 \add ≈towards\add* Yahweh¦53099.
\v 17 Then¦53101 the priest¦53108 must¦53107 put¦53107 some of the remaining¦53101 oil¦53102 on his palm¦53106 onto the lobe¦53111 of the right ear¦53112 of the person being purified¦53113, and on their right thumb¦53117 and right big¦53122 toe¦53122—on top of the blood¦53126 from the guilt¦53127 offering¦53127.
\v 18 Then¦53129 the priest will put¦53136 \add all\add* the remaining¦53129 oil¦53130 from his palm¦53134 onto the head¦53139 of¦53139 the person being purified¦53140, and¦53141 the priest \add ≈will then¦53129 make¦53141 that¦53131 person right with\add* Yahweh¦53145.
\p
\v 19 Then¦53147 the priest¦53148 must¦53147 make the sin¦53151 offering and¦53147 \add ≈make that person right\add* after¦53157 being purified¦53155 from¦53156 their ‘uncleanness¦53156’. After¦53157 that \add ?@that person\add* will¦53158 slaughter \add lamb for\add* the burnt¦53161 offering.
\v 20 Then¦53163 the priest¦53164 must¦53163 offer¦53163 \add &that\add* burnt¦53167 offering and the grain¦53170 offering \add ≈on the fire\add* on the altar¦53171 and he will make¦53172 \add ≈that person right again\add* and he will be¦53175 ‘clean¦53175’.
\p
\v 21 \add ≈However,\add* if¦53178 \add @that person\add* is poor¦53180 and \add ≈cannot afford\add* \add the multiple lambs\add*, then they must¦53185 take¦53185 \em one\em* lamb¦53186 to wave as the guilt¦53188 offering and to make¦53190 \add ≈them right again\add*, along with \em one\em* kilogram of fine¦53193 flour¦53193 mixed¦53195 with oil for the grain¦53197 offering, and the half litre of oil,
\v 22 plus¦53210 two¦53201 doves or¦53203 \add ≈young¦53205\add* pigeons—whichever¦53207 they can afford—one for a sin¦53212 offering and¦53201 the other for the burnt¦53214 offering.
\v 23 Then¦53216 on \add &that\add* eighth¦53219 day¦53218, he'll¦53216 take them¦53217 to the priest¦53223 at the entrance¦53226 of the \add ≈sacred¦53227\add* tent¦53227 for purification¦53220 \add ≈in¦53230 front¦53230\add* of Yahweh¦53231.
\v 24 Then¦53233 the priest¦53234 should take¦53233 the guilt¦53238 offering lamb¦53237 and the \add ≈container\add* of oil¦53242 and lift them¦53244 up as a wave¦53243 offering \add ≈in¦53247 front¦53247\add* of Yahweh¦53248.
\v 25 Then¦53250 \add ?@the person\add* should slaughter \add &that\add* guilt¦53254 offering¦53254 lamb¦53253, and the priest¦53256 must¦53250 take¦53255 some¦53257 of \add ≈that\add* blood¦53257 and put it¦53259 on the lobe¦53262 of the right ear¦53263 of the person being purified¦53265, and on their right thumb¦53269 and right big¦53274 toe¦53274.
\v 26 Then¦53278 \add *he¦53281\add* must¦53281 pour¦53281 some of¦53285 the oil¦53280 onto \add *his\add* left¦53287 palm¦53285
\v 27 and¦53289 with¦53291 his right¦53292 finger¦53291 he must¦53289 \add ≈flick\add* it seven¦53301 times¦53302 \add ≈towards\add* Yahweh¦53304.
\v 28 Then¦53306 the priest¦53307 must put some¦53308 of the oil¦53310 from his¦53315 palm¦53315 onto the lobe¦53318 of the right ear¦53319 of the person being purified¦53320, and on their right thumb¦53324 and right big¦53329 toe¦53329—on top of the blood¦53335 from the guilt¦53336 offering¦53336.
\v 29 Then¦53338 the priest will put¦53347 \add all\add* the remaining¦53338 oil¦53341 from his palm¦53345 onto the head¦53350 of the person being purified¦53351, and¦53338 the priest \add ≈will then¦53338 make¦53352 that¦53342 person right with\add* Yahweh¦53355.
\v 30 Then¦53357 he¦53357 must¦53357 \add ≈offer¦53357\add* one¦53360 of¦53361 the¦53363 birds (dove¦53368 or¦53364 pigeon—whatever \add @that¦53369 person\add* \add ≈could afford\add*)
\v 31 as a sin¦53381 offering and \add ≈the other\add* as a burnt¦53385 offering along with the grain¦53388 offering and he¦53389 will¦53389 make¦53389 \add ≈that¦53374 person right again with\add* Yahweh¦53394.
\v 32 \add The above\add* are the regulations for anyone who has a skin¦53402 disease¦53402 \add ≈but who couldn't afford the regular purification¦53408 offerings\add*.
\s1 Treating contaminated homes
\rem /s1 Cleansing From Mildew; Mildew in Houses; Treatment of Contaminated Houses
\p
\v 33 Then Yahweh¦53412 told Mosheh¦53415 and¦53416 Aharon¦53418:
\p
\v 34 “\add ≈When\add* you enter into¦53423 the¦53425 land of¦53425 Kanaan¦53426 which¦53427 I'm¦53428 giving¦53429 you all as a possession¦53431, and¦53432 if I \add ≈cause\add* an infection in one your¦53437 homes in \add *that¦53427\add* land,
\v 35 then¦53439 the homeowner must¦53439 go and¦53439 inform the priest¦53445 that something like¦53447 an infection has¦53448 appeared¦53448 in¦53450 their house¦53450.
\v 36 The¦53453 priest¦53453 must¦53452 order that everything be removed out of the house before¦53458 \add *he\add* comes to \add ≈inspect it\add* \add ≈so¦53472 that\add* it won't¦53465 all be pronounced as ‘unclean¦53466’. After¦53471 \add ≈that's¦53469 done\add*, he'll¦53452 go¦53473 to see¦53475 the house
\v 37 and \add ≈examine\add* the growth. If¦53484 the growth is greenish¦53489 or¦53490 reddish¦53491 and seems more¦53494 than¦53494 surface deep¦53493,
\v 38 then¦53498 the priest¦53499 must¦53498 leave the house via the \add main\add* entrance¦53505 and¦53498 quarantine the house for seven¦53511 days¦53512.
\v 39 On¦53519 the seventh¦53517 day¦53516, the priest¦53515 must¦53514 return¦53514 and \add ≈examine it¦53520\add* \add again\add*, and if the growth has¦53520 spread¦53520 on the house¦53523 walls¦53522,
\v 40 then¦53525 \add *he¦53525\add* must¦53525 order that those infected stones¦53530 be pulled out¦53527 of the wall and¦53525 thrown¦53534 outside¦53538 the city¦53539 into a place¦53542 \add that's considered\add* ‘unclean¦53543’.
\v 41 Then¦53545 \add the homeowner\add* must¦53548 scrape¦53548 \add ≈all¦53550 the plaster off¦53556 the inside¦53549 walls\add* and¦53551 \add also\add* \add ≈dispose of¦53560 that\add* at \add &that\add* ‘unclean¦53564’ place¦53563.
\v 42 Then¦53566 they \add ≈can replace the stones that were removed\add*, and¦53566 \add ≈apply fresh plaster¦53577\add* to the house¦53580.
\p
\v 43 \add ≈However,\add* if¦53582 the growth returns¦53584 and breaks¦53586 out¦53586 \add again\add* in¦53587 the house¦53587 \add even\add* after¦53588 \add ≈the stones¦53592 were replaced and the walls were replastered\add*,
\v 44 then the priest¦53602 must¦53601 come¦53601 \add back\add* and \add ≈reexamine\add* it. If¦53604 the growth has¦53605 spread¦53605 \add ≈on the walls\add*, then it's¦53610 a malignant¦53609 growth and \add @the house¦53611\add* is¦53612 ‘unclean¦53612’.
\v 45 \add @The owner\add* must tear the house¦53618 down—its stones¦53621 and timber and all¦53626 the mortar, must be \add ≈carted\add* outside¦53633 the city¦53634 into a place¦53637 \add that's considered\add* ‘unclean¦53638’.
\v 46 Any person that enters that house¦53643 \add ≈after the priest had¦53647 quarantined it¦53648\add*, will¦53649 be¦53649 ‘unclean¦53649’ until¦53650 \add &that\add* evening¦53652.
\v 47 Any person who¦53654 lies¦53654 down¦53654 or eats¦53660 in that house, must¦53656 wash their clothes¦53659.
\p
\v 48 \add ≈However¦53673,\add* if¦53667 the priest¦53671 \add ≈came back\add* after the house was replastered and¦53667 \add ≈after his inspection, find that\add* the growth \add ≈hasn't reappeared\add*, then¦53667 \add *he¦53684\add* can pronounce the house as ‘clean’ because¦53689 the \add ≈growth has gone\add*.
\v 49 Then he¦53694 must¦53694 take¦53694 two¦53699 birds¦53700, cedar¦53702 wood, scarlet¦53703 \add ≈thread\add*, and some hyssop¦53705 \add twigs\add*,
\v 50 and¦53707 slaughter one bird¦53710 \add ?≈so the blood runs into¦53712\add* a clay jug \add ?≈containing\add* water¦53719 \add ≈from a spring or creek\add*.
\v 51 Then¦53722 \add ?@the priest\add* must¦53722 take¦53722 the live bird, along with the cedar¦53727 wood¦53725, the scarlet¦53733 \add thread\add*, the hyssop¦53730 \add twigs\add* and the live bird, and dip¦53738 them¦53739 \add ≈all\add* into that¦53742 blood¦53740 of¦53740 the slaughtered bird (\add ?≈mixed with\add* the \add ≈fresh\add* water¦53743), and \add ≈flick\add* it seven¦53749 times¦53750 onto the house¦53748.
\v 52 \add In that way,\add* he'll¦53752 purify the house¦53755 with the bird's¦53757 blood¦53756 and the \add ≈fresh\add* water¦53758, and with the live¦53761 bird and the cedar¦53763 \add wood\add*, the hyssop¦53764 \add twigs\add* and the scarlet¦53765 \add thread\add*.
\v 53 Then¦53768 he¦53768 must¦53768 \add ≈release\add* the live¦53772 bird¦53771 \add to fly\add* into the countryside¦53780, \add ≈thus\add* making¦53781 the house¦53784 \add ≈right with God\add*, and¦53768 then¦53768 it'll¦53785 be¦53785 ‘clean’.
\p
\v 54 \add @The above\add* are the regulations concerning any serious¦53792 skin¦53792 diseases¦53792 and¦53793 itchiness,
\v 55 as well as growths on clothing¦53796 and¦53797 \add ≈buildings\add*
\v 56 and swellings¦53799, rashes, and bright spots \add on the skin\add*,
\v 57 \add ≈so that¦53808 you'll know how to determine what's\add* ‘unclean¦53805’ or ‘clean’. Those are the regulations for \add ≈infectious growths\add*.
\c 15
\s1 Dealing with bodily discharges
\rem /s1 Bodily Discharges; Unclean Bodily Discharges; Discharges Causing Uncleanness; Concerning Bodily Discharges
\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦53814 told Mosheh¦53817 and¦53818 Aaron¦53820:
\p
\v 2 Tell¦53827 the¦53826 \add ≈Israelis¦53826\add* that whenever any man has a discharge¦53834 from¦53835 his \add ≈genitals\add*, then he becomes ‘unclean¦53837’.
\v 3 He becomes ‘unclean’ whether his body¦53845 secretes¦53844 the flow or¦53849 if it's¦53851 blocked—either way he's ‘unclean’.
\v 4 Any bed¦53859 that¦53860 he was lying¦53861 on during \add or after\add* the¦53863 discharge¦53863 becomes ‘unclean¦53864’, as does anything he sits¦53870 on.
\v 5 Anyone¦53874 who¦53875 touches¦53876 that bed¦53877 must¦53876 wash¦53878 their clothes¦53879 and bathe themself in water¦53881, and \add @that person\add* will¦53882 be¦53882 ‘unclean¦53882’ until¦53883 the¦53885 evening¦53885.
\v 6 \add ≈Similarly,\add* anyone¦53887 who¦53887 sits¦53887 on the place where he sat must¦53893 wash¦53896 their clothes¦53897 and bathe themself in water¦53899, and \add @that¦53891 person\add* will¦53900 be¦53900 ‘unclean¦53900’ until¦53901 the evening¦53903.
\v 7 Anyone¦53905 who touches¦53905 the man who had a discharge¦53907 must¦53908 wash¦53908 their clothes¦53909 and bathe themself in water¦53911, and \add @that person\add* will¦53912 be¦53912 ‘unclean¦53912’ until¦53913 the evening¦53915.
\v 8 If that man who had a discharge¦53920 spits¦53919 on¦53921 some person who was ‘clean’, then¦53917 \add @that person\add* must¦53919 wash¦53922 their clothes¦53923 and bathe themself in water¦53925, and they'll be¦53926 ‘unclean¦53926’ until¦53927 the¦53929 evening¦53929.
\v 9 Any thing that¦53934 the¦53933 man who had a discharge¦53937 rides¦53935 on¦53936, will¦53938 become ‘unclean¦53938’,
\v 10 and anyone who touches¦53942 it¦53945 will be ‘unclean’ until the evening, plus¦53951 anyone who \add ≈carries¦53951 any of those things\add*, must¦53945 wash their clothes¦53954 and bathe themself in water¦53956, and they'll be ‘unclean’ until the evening.
\v 11 Anyone the \add ≈man who had¦53971 a discharge¦53967\add* touches¦53964 and do didn't¦53969 rinse¦53971 their hands¦53968 in water, must¦53964 wash¦53973 their clothes¦53974 and bathe themself in water, and they'll be¦53977 ‘unclean¦53977’ until¦53978 the evening¦53980.
\v 12 Any container that¦53985 the¦53990 \add ≈man who had a discharge¦53990\add* touches¦53987, must¦53987 be¦53991 \add ≈smashed\add* if it's \add ≈made from\add* clay and¦53992 rinsed¦53997 with¦53998 water¦53998 if it's \add ≈made from\add* wood¦53996.
\p
\v 13 When¦54000 the¦54003 \add ≈man's discharge¦54003 ceases\add*, he must mark off seven¦54007 days¦54008 for¦54009 his purification¦54009, and then¦54000 he must wash¦54010 his clothes¦54011 and bathe himself in water¦54014, and \add after that,\add* he'll¦54002 be¦54016 ‘clean’.
\v 14 Then¦54018 on¦54018 the eighth¦54019 day¦54018, he must¦54020 take¦54020 two¦54023 doves or¦54025 \add ≈young¦54027\add* pigeons, and¦54018 \add ≈stand in front¦54031\add* of Yahweh¦54032 at the entrance¦54035 to the \add ≈sacred¦54036\add* tent¦54036. There he should give¦54038 them¦54038 to a priest¦54041,
\v 15 and the priest¦54045 must¦54043 \add ≈offer¦54043\add* one as a sin¦54047 offering and \add ≈the other\add* as a burnt¦54049 offering, \add ≈thus making¦54050 the man right\add* with Yahweh¦54054 for his¦54055 discharge¦54055.
\p
\v 16 \add ≈Now\add* when a man¦54058 has an \add ≈emission of¦54063 semen\add*, then he must¦54061 bathe his¦54072 entire¦54070 body¦54072 in water¦54067, and¦54073 he'll¦54066 be¦54073 ‘unclean¦54073’ until¦54074 the¦54076 evening¦54076.
\v 17 He must¦54086 also wash¦54091 all his clothing, and any leather articles on¦54087 him¦54087 \add ≈that came into contact with¦54092 the semen\add* and \add @all of¦54088 that\add* will¦54093 be¦54093 ‘unclean¦54093’ until¦54094 the evening¦54096.
\v 18 \add ≈When a man¦54102 and a woman¦54099 ‘sleep together’\add*, then they must¦54101 both bathe in water¦54108, and they'll¦54107 \add both\add* be¦54109 ‘unclean¦54109’ until¦54110 the¦54112 evening¦54112.\f + \fr 15:18 \ft Note that if they had sexual relations in the evening, say 9pm, then they'd be ‘unclean’ all the next day and until the \+em following\+em* evening (because the Jewish ‘day’ begins after dusk—rather than at midnight like modern Western society counts time).\f*
\p
\v 19 When¦54114 a woman¦54114 \add ≈has her menstrual¦54126 period\add*, she'll¦54117 be ‘unclean’ for seven¦54123 days¦54124, and¦54114 anyone¦54129 who¦54129 touches¦54129 her \add ≈during that time¦54124\add* will¦54131 be ‘unclean’ until¦54132 the¦54134 evening¦54134.
\v 20 Anything that she¦54138 lies¦54138 on or sits¦54145 on \add ≈during that time\add* will become ‘unclean¦54147’.
\v 21 Anyone¦54151 who¦54151 touches¦54151 her¦54152 bed¦54152 must¦54153 wash¦54153 their clothes¦54154 and bathe in water¦54156, and they'll be¦54157 ‘unclean¦54157’ until¦54158 the¦54160 evening¦54160.
\v 22 Anyone¦54164 who¦54164 touches¦54164 anything that¦54168 she¦54170 sat¦54170 on¦54171 must¦54170 wash¦54172 their clothes¦54173 and bathe in water¦54175, and they'll be¦54176 ‘unclean¦54176’ until¦54177 the¦54179 evening¦54179,
\v 23 \add ≈i.e.,\add* whether it's¦54185 her bed¦54184 or¦54186 something she¦54192 sat¦54193 on, anyone who touches¦54196 it will¦54199 be¦54199 ‘unclean¦54199’ until¦54200 the¦54202 evening¦54202.
\v 24 If¦54204 a man¦54207 \add ≈sleeps with\add* \add @a menstruating¦54210 woman\add* and \add ≈gets blood\add* on him¦54211, then¦54204 he'll¦54206 be¦54212 ‘unclean’ for seven¦54213 days¦54214, and any bed¦54217 that¦54218 he lies on will¦54222 \add also\add* become ‘unclean’.
\p
\v 25 If¦54226 any woman¦54225 \add ≈has a blood¦54230 flow when it's¦54228 not¦54233 her period\add*, or¦54237 \add ≈keeps bleeding beyond her menstrual¦54243 period\add*, all¦54244 \add ≈those\add* days \add ≈will be regarded the same as her menstruation¦54250 so she'll¦54240 be\add* ‘unclean¦54248’.
\v 26 Any bed¦54257 that¦54258 she lies¦54260 on \add ≈as long as she's discharging¦54265 blood will be regarded the same as during her¦54264 menstruation¦54267 and¦54271 will\add* be ‘unclean¦54277’, as will anything she sits¦54275 on.
\v 27 \add ≈Also¦54282,\add* any person who¦54284 touches¦54284 them¦54285 will¦54286 be ‘unclean’ and they must¦54286 wash¦54287 their clothes¦54288 and bathe in water¦54290, and they'll be ‘unclean’ until¦54292 the¦54294 evening¦54294.
\v 28 \add ≈Once the flow stops,\add* then \add @the woman\add* must¦54300 count¦54300 off seven¦54302 days¦54303, and¦54296 then she'll¦54300 be¦54305 ‘clean’ after¦54304 that.
\v 29 Then¦54307 on¦54307 the eighth¦54308 day¦54307, she¦54309 must¦54309 take¦54309 two¦54312 doves or¦54314 \add ≈young¦54316\add* pigeons and¦54307 \add ≈give them¦54319\add* to a priest¦54322 at the entrance¦54325 to the \add ≈sacred¦54326\add* tent¦54326,
\v 30 and he¦54329 will¦54329 offer¦54329 one¦54333 as a sin¦54334 offering and \add ≈the¦54337 other\add* as a burnt¦54338 offering, \add ≈thus making¦54339 her right with\add* Yahweh¦54343 from¦54344 her ‘unclean¦54345’ flow.
\p
\v 31 You¦54352 two must¦54347 keep¦54347 the¦54350 \add ≈Israeli¦54350 people¦54350\add* separate¦54347 from¦54353 their ‘uncleanness¦54357’, then¦54347 they¦54355 won't¦54354 defile my¦54360 residence that's among¦54362 them¦54362, and¦54347 cause their \add own\add* death.
\p
\v 32 \add ≈The¦54365 above\add* are the¦54366 regulations for any man with a discharge¦54366 or a seminal emission that¦54367 makes him¦54369 ‘unclean¦54373’,
\v 33 plus¦54379 any woman who is menstruating¦54377 or has a bodily discharge¦54379, as well as any man¦54385 who sleeps with¦54388 an¦54390 ‘unclean¦54390’ woman.
\c 16
\s1 The day for making things right
\rem /s1 The Day of Atonement
\p
\v 1 Yahweh spoke¦54393 to¦54395 Mosheh¦54397 after¦54398 the death¦54399 of two¦54400 of Aharon's¦54402 sons¦54401 when¦54403 they¦54403 approached Yahweh \add wrongly\add* and¦54407 died¦54407,
\v 2 and¦54438 \add *he\add* told Mosheh¦54413:
\p Tell¦54410 your brother¦54418 Aharon¦54417 that if he doesn't \add want to\add* die¦54439, then¦54409 he mustn't \add just\add* enter the \add ≈holiest room¦54427\add* inside¦54428 the curtain¦54429 at any old time¦54424. The¦54433 atonement¦54433 lid is¦54435 on¦54435 the \add sacred\add* box¦54437, and I¦54442 will¦54439 appear¦54442 in¦54441 a cloud¦54441 over¦54443 \add *that\add* lid.\x + \xo 16:2: \xt Heb 6:19.\x*
\p
\v 3 This¦54447 is \add how\add* Aharon¦54449 must enter the \add ≈sacred¦54452 tent\add*: \add he must acquire\add* a \add ≈young¦54454\add* bull¦54453 for a sin¦54457 offering, and¦54458 a ram¦54458 for a burnt¦54459 offering.
\v 4 ⇔He must bathe himself¦54475 in water¦54484 and then put¦54488 on linen underclothes¦54466, followed by his sacred linen tunic¦54461 and tie the linen sash¦54473 around it. Then he must wrap the linen turban¦54476 on. Those are \add all\add* sacred clothes¦54479.
\p
\v 5 Then¦54493 \add @Aharon\add* must¦54494 \add acquire\add* two¦54495 \add ≈young\add* goats for a sin¦54499 offering and¦54490 one¦54501 ram¦54500 for a burnt¦54502 offering.
\v 6 \add *He¦54504\add* must¦54504 present¦54504 the bull¦54508 as a sin¦54509 offering¦54509 for himself¦54514 to¦54512 \add ≈make¦54513 both him¦54512 and¦54504 his¦54516 household¦54516 right with God¦54505\add*.
\v 7 Then¦54518 he¦54518 must¦54518 take¦54518 the two¦54521 goats¦54522 and¦54518 make them¦54524 stand \add ≈in¦54525 front¦54525\add* of¦54525 Yahweh¦54526 at the entrance¦54527 to¦54525 the \add ≈sacred¦54528\add* tent¦54528,
\v 8 and \add ≈throw dice to decide which\add* one is for¦54540 Yahweh¦54540, and one is to be the¦54543 ‘scapegoat’.
\v 9 Then¦54545 Aharon¦54546 must¦54545 present¦54545 the goat¦54549 that's for¦54554 Yahweh¦54554, and¦54545 offer¦54555 it¦54555 as a sin¦54556 offering¦54556,
\v 10 \add ≈but¦54558\add* the \add ≈chosen\add* ‘scapegoat’ must¦54564 be kept standing there \add ≈in¦54567 front¦54567\add* of¦54567 Yahweh, \add ≈because it'll¦54564 be used to make¦54569 the people right with Yahweh\add*, \add and be sent\add* into the wilderness¦54574.
\p
\v 11 Then¦54576 Aharon¦54577 must¦54576 present¦54576 the bull for his own sin offering \add ≈to¦54584 make¦54585 him¦54584 and¦54576 his household¦54588 right with God\add*, then¦54576 he'll¦54576 slaughter the bull for the sin offering for himself¦54586.
\v 12 Then¦54598 he¦54598 must¦54598 get a panful of burning¦54604 coals¦54602 off the altar¦54606 \add ≈in front¦54607\add* of Yahweh¦54608 as well as two handfuls of finely-ground, fragrant incense¦54611, and¦54598 take¦54598 them inside¦54615 the curtain¦54616
\v 13 where he'll¦54639 put the incense on the \add ≈coals\add* in¦54625 Yahweh's¦54626 \add ≈presence\add*. Then¦54618 the \add smoke\add* cloud¦54629 from the incense will cover¦54633 the atonement¦54633 lid on the \add sacred\add* chest, and¦54618 he won't¦54638 die¦54639.
\v 14 Then¦54641 he must take¦54641 some¦54642 of the bull's blood, and¦54641 using his finger¦54645, he must flick the blood seven¦54654 times¦54656 onto the eastern the side of the lid and seven times onto the front¦54648 of the lid.
\p
\v 15 Then¦54662 \add @Aharon\add* must¦54662 slaughter the goat¦54665 for the people's¦54668 sin¦54666 offering¦54666, and take its blood inside¦54675 the curtain¦54676, and do¦54677 the same with¦54678 it that¦54667 he¦54682 did¦54682 to¦54683 the bull's¦54684 blood—\add ≈flicking\add* it onto the side and front¦54690 of¦54690 the atonement¦54691 lid,\x + \xo 16:15: \xt Heb 9:12.\x*
\v 16 \add ≈thus\add* making¦54693 the \add ≈Israeli¦54698 people\add* \add ≈right with Yahweh\add* for their uncleanness and their \add ≈rebellion and disobedience\add*. \add ≈That's also for\add* the \add ≈sacred¦54696\add* tent¦54706 which¦54708 is among \add @the people\add* with their uncleanness.
\v 17 \add ≈No one else can enter\add* the \add ≈sacred\add* tent¦54720 when¦54722 \add @Aharon\add* enters to¦54723 make atonement in¦54724 the \add ≈sacred room¦54724\add* until¦54725 he¦54727 leaves \add again\add*. He¦54728 must¦54718 make atonement for himself¦54729 and¦54713 his¦54731 household¦54731, as well as for the whole¦54713 \add ≈Israeli¦54735 community\add*,
\v 18 then¦54738 he'll¦54738 go¦54738 out¦54738 to¦54739 the altar that's \add ≈in¦54743 front¦54743\add* of Yahweh¦54745 and make¦54746 atonement¦54746 for that—he must¦54738 take¦54748 some of the bull's¦54750 blood and some of the goat's¦54752 blood and put it¦54753 on¦54754 the \add four\add* \add ≈projecting corners\add* of the altar.
\v 19 Then¦54760 he¦54760 must¦54760 \add ≈flick\add* blood¦54764 on¦54761 to it seven¦54766 times¦54767 with¦54765 his¦54765 finger¦54765, thus purifying¦54768 it and¦54760 \add ≈removing\add* the uncleanness¦54770 of¦54770 the \add ≈Israeli¦54771 people¦54771 from it\add*.
\s1 The goat taking the blame
\rem /s1 The Scapegoat
\p
\v 20 \add ≈When¦54774\add* \add @Aharon\add* has finished¦54774 purifying the sacred \add ≈room¦54778\add*, the \add ≈sacred\add* tent¦54781, and¦54774 the altar¦54785, then¦54774 he¦54786 should present¦54786 the live¦54790 goat¦54789.
\v 21 \add *He¦54793\add* must place \add ≈both¦54796\add* his¦54797 hands¦54797 on¦54799 the goat's head, and confess¦54803 all of Israel's¦54811 \add ≈disobedience, rebellion, and shortcomings\add*—\add symbolically\add* placing them¦54821 onto the goat's head, and then¦54792 he¦54826 must choose a man¦54829 \add ≈that's nearby\add* to¦54831 take it into the wilderness¦54831.
\v 22 ⇔Then¦54833 he'll¦54845 release the goat there in the wilderness¦54849, and¦54833 the goat will carry all their¦54840 sins into that barren land¦54843.
\p
\v 23 Then¦54851 Aharon¦54852 must¦54851 enter the \add ≈sacred\add* tent¦54855 and take off¦54857 the linen¦54861 garment¦54860 that¦54862 he'd put on as he'd entered into¦54865 the sacred \add ≈room¦54867\add* and leave¦54868 them¦54868 there¦54869.\x + \xo 16:23: \xt Eze 44:19.\x*
\v 24 Then¦54871 he¦54871 must¦54871 wash¦54871 himself in water¦54875 in a sacred¦54877 place¦54876, put¦54878 on¦54878 his \add regular\add* clothes¦54881, and go out¦54882 and make¦54891 his burnt offering and the burnt offering for the people, \add ≈thus making both himself and the people right with Yahweh\add*.
\v 25 Then¦54896 he must¦54899 burn the fat¦54897 from the sin¦54898 offering¦54898 up on the altar¦54900.
\v 26 \add ≈Also¦54902,\add* the person who¦54902 led away the ‘scapegoat’ must¦54907 wash¦54907 his¦54908 clothes¦54908 and bathe himself in water¦54913, and then¦54902 he¦54917 can reenter the camp¦54920.
\v 27 Then¦54922 \add the remains of\add* the bull¦54923 and the goat¦54927 from the sin¦54928 offerings¦54928 (whose blood¦54933 was¦54930 taken into the sacred \add ≈room¦54935\add* to make¦54934 atonement¦54934) must be taken to a place¦54935 outside¦54939 the camp¦54940 where they must be burnt¦54941—skins, flesh¦54948, and dung.\x + \xo 16:27: \xt Heb 13:11.\x*
\v 28 The¦54953 man who¦54953 burnt¦54953 them¦54954 must¦54955 then wash¦54955 his clothes¦54956 and bathe his body¦54960 in water¦54961, and then he¦54965 can reenter the¦54968 camp¦54968.
\s1 The national purification day
\rem /s1 Observing the Day of Atonement
\p
\v 29 This will¦54970 be a permanent¦54973 regulation¦54972 for¦54971 you all¦54982:
\p On the 10th of the seventh¦54975 month¦54977 \add (of Tishrei—around September/October)\add*, all of you including¦54982 those who are native-born¦54987 as well as foreigners living among¦54990 you, must¦54970 humble yourselves and¦54970 not \add ≈work¦54984 that day\add*\x + \xo 16:29-34: \xt Lev 23:26-32; Num 29:7-11.\x*
\v 30 because¦54992 on¦54994 that¦54995 day¦54994, \add @the¦54995 high priest\add* will¦54996 purify¦54998 you all from your sins¦55001 \add ≈to¦55002 make¦54996 you right with\add* Yahweh¦55003, and you'll be¦55004 ‘clean’.
\v 31 It'll be a \add ≈very sacred\add* rest day for you, and¦55010 you all must¦55010 humble \add ≈yourselves\add*—a permanent¦55015 regulation¦55014 \add for you all\add*.
\v 32 The¦55018 priest \add ≈who's anointed¦55021 and ordained to succeed\add* his father¦55030 \add as high priest\add* must \add ≈be the one to\add* make¦55017 atonement¦55017, and he¦55031 must be wearing¦55031 his \add ≈sacred¦55037\add* linen¦55035 clothes¦55034.
\v 33 He¦55039 will¦55039 \add first\add* \add ≈purify\add* the \add ≈sacred room\add* and the \add ≈sacred\add* tent¦55046, and the altar¦55050, and then¦55039 \add ≈make all the priests¦55053 right with Yahweh\add* and \add finally,\add* the \add ≈entire¦55056 community\add*.
\v 34 That will¦55062 become¦55062 a permanent¦55067 regulation¦55066 every year¦55077 to \add ≈make¦55068 all the Israelis¦55071 right with Yahweh¦55081 because of\add* their¦55075 sins¦55075.
\p \add ≈So¦55062\add* Mosheh¦55084 did exactly as¦55079 Yahweh had¦55080 instructed¦55080 him.
\c 17
\s1 Slaughtering animals
\rem /s1 The Slaughtering of Animals; Law of holiness; Prohibitions against Eating Blood; The Sacredness of Blood; Eating Blood Forbidden
\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦55088 told¦55092 Mosheh¦55091:
\p
\v 2 Tell¦55105 Aharon¦55097 and his¦55100 sons¦55100 and all¦55102 the \add ≈Israelis¦55104\add* that¦55110 \add ≈these are the instructions¦55112 from\add* Yahweh¦55113:
\v 3 \add ≈No Israeli¦55119 is allowed to\add* slaughter a bull¦55122 or lamb or goat¦55128 \add either\add* inside the camp or outside¦55133 \add *it\add*.
\v 4 \add ≈If¦55148 they're not taken\add* to the entrance¦55138 to the \add ≈sacred¦55139\add* tent¦55147 to be presented as an offering to Yahweh¦55145 \add ≈in¦55146 front¦55146\add* of \add *his\add* residence, then¦55136 that person¦55151 \add ≈will¦55150 be held guilty\add* of its blood—they've shed¦55154 blood so they must¦55150 be cut¦55155 off¦55155 from¦55158 his people¦55159.
\v 5 The¦55164 \add ≈Israelis¦55164\add* \add ≈must stop\add* sacrificing¦55171 their¦55168 \add ≈animals\add* in the countryside¦55175, and \add instead\add* bring them to Yahweh at the entrance¦55180 to the \add ≈sacred¦55181\add* tent¦55181, \add i.e., they must\add* bring them to the priest¦55185 and sacrifice¦55186 them as peace¦55188 offerings¦55188 to Yahweh.
\v 6 Then¦55192 the priest¦55193 will splash the blood¦55196 onto Yahweh's¦55200 altar¦55199 at the tent¦55202 entrance¦55201, and¦55204 burn up the fat¦55205 to become a \add ≈soothing¦55207 aroma¦55206\add* for¦55208 Yahweh.
\v 7 Then¦55210 they \add ≈won't¦55210 be able to continue offering\add* their¦55216 sacrifices¦55212 to the goat demons that¦55218 they're¦55219 prostituting¦55220 themselves¦55220 to. \add ≈The above\add* will¦55224 be a permanent¦55223 regulation¦55222 \add ≈throughout\add* the generations¦55228.
\p
\v 8 You must¦55231 tell them that if an \add ≈Israeli¦55235\add* or a foreigner living among¦55242 them, makes a burnt¦55246 offering¦55246 or sacrifice¦55249
\v 9 without bringing¦55257 it to Yahweh¦55260 at the \add ≈sacred¦55254\add* tent¦55254 entrance¦55253, then¦55251 that person must¦55257 be cut¦55261 off from \add ≈the community\add*.
\s1 The law concerning the blood
\rem /s1 Eating Blood Prohibited
\p
\v 10 \add If there's\add* any \add ≈Israeli¦55269\add* or foreigner living among¦55274 them, who eats¦55283 blood¦55279, then¦55266 I'll¦55280 \add ≈oppose\add* that person¦55282 and¦55266 remove them from¦55289 \add ≈the¦55289 community\add*\x + \xo 17:10: \xt Gen 9:4; Lev 7:26-27; 19:26; Deu 12:16,23; 15:23.\x*
\v 11 because the body's life is¦55295 in¦55295 the blood. I¦55297 myself have¦55298 given¦55298 you \add @blood\add* to¦55299 make¦55303 atonement¦55303 for your lives at the altar¦55302, because \add ≈it's the blood that¦55311 can atone for\add* life.\x + \xo 17:11: \xt Heb 9:22.\x*
\v 12 \add ≈That's¦55319 why\add* I¦55317 told the \add ≈Israelis¦55318\add* that none of them must¦55326 eat blood—\add not even\add* the foreigners that live among¦55330 them may eat blood.
\p
\v 13 \add ≈So any person\add* (\add ≈Israeli¦55340\add* or¦55350 foreigner living among¦55345 them¦55345) who¦55346 catches wild game¦55348 (\add ≈including¦55337\add* birds) to eat¦55354, they must¦55347 pour¦55355 its¦55358 blood¦55358 out¦55355 and¦55359 cover¦55359 it¦55359 with¦55360 soil
\v 14 because the life of \add ≈their bodies\add* is the blood that's in them. \add ≈Again¦55373,\add* \add that's why\add* I've¦55371 told the \add ≈Israelis¦55372\add* not to eat the blood of any¦55375 \add ≈living thing\add* because the life is in the blood, and¦55371 anyone who¦55389 eats it¦55389 must¦55390 be¦55390 cut¦55390 off¦55390 \add ≡from the community\add*.
\p
\v 15 Anyone who¦55395 eats¦55396 \add part of\add* a carcass¦55397 \add they found\add* or one that was \add ≈killed by wild animals¦55398\add*, must¦55396 wash their clothes¦55402 and bathe in water¦55404, and they'll be ‘unclean¦55405’ until¦55406 the¦55408 evening¦55408, and then¦55392 they'll be ‘clean’ \add again\add*.
\v 16 \add ≈However,\add* if¦55411 \add @that person\add* doesn't wash \add their clothes\add* or bathe, then¦55411 they must¦55413 bear¦55417 \add the punishment for\add* their own \add ≈disobedience\add*.
\c 18
\s1 Sexual relationships
\rem /s1 Unlawful Sexual Relations; Forbidden Sexual Practices; Sexual Relations
\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦55422 told¦55426 Mosheh¦55425:
\p
\v 2 Tell¦55432 the¦55431 \add ≈Israeli¦55431\add* that I¦55435 am¦55436 their god¦55437 Yahweh¦55436.
\v 3 \add ≈They mustn't behave as if they're still there¦55457 in\add* Egypt¦55442, nor should they \add ≈behave like the Canaanites that were living\add* in the land that I'm¦55454 taking you all into, and don't¦55447 \add ≈emulate their¦55460 customs and practices\add*.
\v 4 You all must¦55467 \add ≈imbibe my values and¦55468 follow my instructions¦55470\add*. I¦55474 am¦55475 your god¦55476 Yahweh¦55475.
\v 5 You all must¦55478 \add ≈follow my instructions¦55481 and¦55478 my values\add*—those who do¦55486 so will live¦55489. I¦55491 am¦55492 your god Yahweh¦55492.\x + \xo 18:5: \xt Neh 9:29; Eze 18:9; 20:11-13; Luk 10:28; Rom 10:5; Gal 3:12.\x*
\p
\v 6 None of you may \add ≈ever flirt with any close¦55504 relative¦55501 to try to get them to undress\add*. I¦55507 am¦55508 Yahweh¦55508.
\v 7 You¦55512 must¦55512 \add ≈never mess with your father's¦55512 naked body\add*, or your mother's¦55514—no, she's¦55518 your mother so don't¦55515 \add ≈ever take advantage of¦55521 her¦55521 nakedness¦55521\add*.
\v 8 Don't¦55528 \add ≈ever mess with any of your father's¦55527 wives, because their naked bodies are the realm\add* of your father.\x + \xo 18:8: \xt Lev 20:11; Deu 22:30; 27:20.\x*
\v 9 Don't¦55539 \add ≈flirt with your sister's nakedness¦55535, whether she's a full sister, a half sister, or an adopted sister\add*.\x + \xo 18:9: \xt Lev 20:17; Deu 27:22.\x*
\v 10 Don't¦55562 \add ≈flirt with your grandchildren's nakedness, because¦55565 you'd be absolutely shaming yourself\add*.
\v 11 Don't¦55579 \add ≈flirt with your step-sister's\add* nakedness, because she's your sister and her¦55581 nakedness \add ≈isn't¦55579 yours to enjoy\add*.
\v 12 Don't¦55588 \add ≈flirt with your aunts nakedness¦55584 on your father's¦55587 side\add*, because \add ≈she's¦55592 closely related¦55590 to\add* your father.\x + \xo 18:12-14: \xt Lev 20:19-20.\x*
\v 13 Don't¦55599 \add ≈flirt with your aunt's nakedness¦55595 on your mother's¦55598 side\add*, because¦55601 \add ≈she's closely related¦55603 to\add* your mother.
\v 14 Don't¦55611 \add ≈flirt with your uncle's nakedness¦55608 on your father's¦55611 side\add*, and \add ≈keep away\add* from his wife¦55616, because she's your aunt¦55619.
\v 15 Don't¦55625 \add ≈flirt with\add* your daughter-in-law's¦55624 nakedness, because she's¦55629 your son's¦55628 wife¦55627 and her¦55632 nakedness \add ≈isn't¦55625 yours to enjoy\add*.\x + \xo 18:15: \xt Lev 20:12.\x*
\v 16 Don't¦55639 \add ≈flirt with\add* your sister-in-law, because \add ≈her naked body is¦55641 the¦55641 realm\add* of¦55641 your brother.\x + \xo 18:16: \xt Lev 20:21.\x*
\v 17 Don't¦55649 \add ≈flirt with\add* the¦55646 nakedness¦55646 of¦55646 \add both\add* a woman¦55647 and¦55648 her daughter \add ≈or her granddaughter\add*, because they're \add ≈related¦55665 to each other\add*—that would be perverse.\x + \xo 18:17: \xt Lev 20:14; Deu 27:23.\x*
\v 18 Don't¦55674 take¦55675 your wife's sister¦55673 \add ≈to be a junior wife\add* \add ≈while your wife is still alive\add*.
\p
\v 19 Don't¦55687 approach a woman¦55684 \add ≈who's menstruating¦55685, to undress her¦55685\add*, because she's ‘unclean¦55686’.\x + \xo 18:19: \xt Lev 20:18.\x*
\v 20 Don't¦55696 sleep with \add ≈someone else's\add* wife¦55694—your \add ≈child with her¦55703 would be¦55701\add* ‘unclean¦55701’.\x + \xo 18:20: \xt Lev 20:10.\x*
\v 21 Don't¦55706 \add ≈sacrifice your children\add* to Molek¦55710 so you¦55712 don't¦55706 profane¦55712 your god's¦55716 \add ≈reputation¦55715\add*. I¦55717 am¦55718 Yahweh¦55718.\x + \xo 18:21: \xt Lev 20:1-5.\x*
\v 22 Don't¦55723 \add ≈have sexual relations\add* with a man like with a woman¦55726—it's an¦55727 abomination¦55727.\x + \xo 18:22: \xt Lev 20:13.\x*
\v 23 \add Men,\add* don't \add ≈have sexual relations\add* with any animal as that would make you¦55735 ‘unclean¦55737’. And¦55740 women, don't give¦55735 yourself \add ≈sexually\add* to¦55744 any animal as that's perverse.\x + \xo 18:23: \xt Exo 22:19; Lev 20:15-16; Deu 27:21.\x*
\p
\v 24 Don't¦55750 make¦55752 yourselves¦55752 ‘unclean¦55752’ in¦55753 any of \add @the above\add* ways, because¦55756 all of those¦55755 things were done by the \add ≈people groups\add* that¦55762 I'm¦55764 \add ≈driving out\add* of this land ahead¦55766 of you all.
\v 25 The¦55769 land had become¦55768 ‘unclean¦55768’ \add ≈so I¦55770 made them pay for their wickedness\add* and¦55768 \add so\add* the¦55774 land will vomit¦55773 out its¦55777 inhabitants¦55777.
\v 26 \add ≈However,\add* you all must¦55779 \add ≈obey my¦55783 instructions¦55783 and decisions¦55783\add* and not \add ≈tolerate\add* any of \add ≈that perverse behaviour\add*—not you who are native-born¦55792, nor any foreigner living among¦55795 you all,
\v 27 because¦55797 all \add ≈that perversity\add* was done¦55804 by those¦55803 living there before¦55809 you all, and¦55810 the¦55811 land¦55811 became¦55810 ‘unclean¦55810’.
\v 28 \add Don't think\add* that the land¦55816 won't¦55813 vomit¦55815 you all out just¦55820 like it's¦55821 doing to the \add ≈people groups\add* that have been \add there\add* before¦55826 you,
\v 29 because¦55828 everyone¦55829 who does any of \add ≈those¦55835 perversities\add* will be¦55836 cut¦55836 off¦55836 from¦55839 their¦55840 \add ≈community\add*.
\v 30 \add ≈So¦55842\add* you all must¦55842 carefully guard against \add ≈practising any of those detestable customs¦55848\add* which were \add ≈previously\add* done¦55851 \add there\add* and¦55842 which would make¦55854 you all ‘unclean¦55854’. I¦55856 am¦55857 your god¦55858 Yahweh¦55857.
\c 19
\s1 Various moral imperatives
\rem /s1 Ritual and Moral Holiness; Various Laws; Laws of Holiness and Justice; Holiness in Personal Conduct
\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦55862 told¦55866 Mosheh¦55865:
\p
\v 2 Tell¦55876 the \add ≈entire¦55871 Israeli¦55874 community\add* that they must¦55877 \add ≈be¦55880 separate from others\add*, because¦55881 I¦55883, your god¦55885 Yahweh¦55884, am¦55882 holy¦55882 \add (i.e., separated from impurity)\add*.\x + \xo 19:2: \xt Lev 11:44-45; 1Pe 1:16.\x*
\v 3 Everyone must¦55890 \add ≈respect and obey\add* their \add ≈parents¦55888\add*, and observe my¦55893 rest days. I¦55895 am¦55896 your god¦55897 Yahweh¦55896.\x + \xo 19:3: a \xt Exo 20:12; Deu 5:16; \xo b \xt Exo 20:8; Deu 5:12.\x*
\p
\v 4 Don't¦55899 turn¦55901 to¦55902 worthless¦55904 idols¦55904, and¦55905 don't¦55899 make¦55908 cast metal¦55906 gods¦55905 for¦55909 yourselves. I¦55910 am¦55911 your god¦55912 Yahweh¦55911.\x + \xo 19:4: a \xt Lev 26:1; \xo b \xt Exo 20:23; 34:17; Deu 27:15.\x*
\p
\v 5 When¦55918 you all sacrifice peace¦55917 offerings¦55917, \add ≈do it¦55920 correctly so that you'll all be accepted¦55919\add*.
\v 6 \add The meat from\add* your¦55923 sacrifice¦55923 must be eaten¦55924 that same day or the next¦55925 day—anything left until¦55927 the third¦55930 day must be \add ≈thrown into the fire¦55931\add*.
\v 7 If¦55934 it was to be eaten¦55936 on the third¦55938 day¦55937, it would be ‘unclean¦55939’ and¦55934 not acceptable¦55942,
\v 8 and the people eating¦55944 it would have¦55953 to bear¦55946 their own \add ≈guilt\add* for profaning¦55953 Yahweh's¦55952 holiness, and that¦55956 person must¦55946 be¦55954 cut¦55954 off¦55954 from¦55957 \add ≈the community\add*.
\p
\v 9 When¦55959 you all harvest your \add ≈crops off\add* your land¦55963, you mustn't \add ≈cut the grain right to¦55968 the very\add* edge of your field¦55967, and¦55959 nor \add ≈can you all pick up any dropped stalks\add*.\x + \xo 19:9-10: \xt Lev 27:15; Deu 24:19-22.\x*
\v 10 In your \add #vineyards\add*, you must not \add ≈pick every last grape¦55977 or pick up any that fall¦55977 on the ground\add*, because they must be left¦55983 for the poor and¦55974 for the foreigners. I¦55985 am¦55986 your god¦55987 Yahweh¦55986.
\p
\v 11 You all mustn't steal¦55990 or deceive¦55993, or defraud any fellow¦55998 citizen¦55998,\x + \xo 19:11: a \xt Exo 20:15; Deu 5:19; \xo b \xt Exo 20:16; Deu 5:20.\x*
\v 12 and don't¦56000 use my name to¦56004 \add ≈seal\add* a promise and then¦56000 \add go ahead and\add* \add ≈ruin my reputation¦56003\add*. I¦56010 am¦56011 Yahweh¦56011.\x + \xo 19:12: \xt Exo 20:7; Deu 5:11; Mat 5:33.\x*
\p
\v 13 Don't oppress¦56015 your¦56018 \add #neighbours¦56018\add* or steal from them. Don't \add ≈fail to pay a day-labourer as they finish each day's work\add*.\x + \xo 19:13: \xt Deu 24:14-15.\x*
\v 14 Don't¦56037 curse¦56033 a deaf¦56034 person, or \add ≈put¦56038 something in front¦56035 of¦56035\add* a blind¦56036 person \add to trip them\add*. You¦56038 must¦56033 \add ≈respect and¦56040 obey\add* your¦56041 god¦56041. I¦56042 am¦56043 Yahweh¦56043.\x + \xo 19:14: \xt Deu 27:18.\x*
\p
\v 15 Don't¦56050 judge unfairly—showing partiality to the poor¦56055, or honouring¦56057 those who are well-known—you must¦56047 \add always\add* judge your¦56062 fellow¦56062 citizens¦56062 fairly.\x + \xo 19:15: \xt Exo 23:6-8; Deu 16:19.\x*
\v 16 Don't go¦56066 around slandering¦56067 people. Don't \add ?≈take advantage of your¦56074 neighbour's¦56074 death\add*. I¦56075 am¦56076 Yahweh¦56076.
\p
\v 17 You¦56080 mustn't hate¦56080 your¦56084 brother¦56083. Certainly rebuke¦56085 \add ≈those you interact with\add* \add ≈so you don't¦56090 get blamed for their bad behaviour\add*.\x + \xo 19:17: \xt Mat 18:15.\x*
\v 18 Don't¦56099 try to¦56107 get revenge against others or hold a grudge against any of¦56107 your people¦56105, but¦56099 \add instead,\add* love¦56106 your neighbour¦56107 as yourself¦56108. I¦56109 am¦56110 Yahweh¦56110.\x + \xo 19:18: \xt Mat 5:43; 19:19; 22:39; Mrk 12:31; Luk 10:27; Rom 13:9; Gal 5:14; Jam 2:8.\x*
\p
\v 19 \add ≈Follow my¦56114 instructions¦56114\add*—don't crossbreed two different kinds of animals, don't sow¦56124 two different crops in your field¦56121, and¦56126 don't wear clothing¦56126 made¦56119 of different kinds of thread.\x + \xo 19:19: \xt Deu 22:9-11.\x*
\p
\v 20 If¦56135 a man¦56147 impregnates a woman¦56140 who's destined to be someone else's slave¦56145 and she hasn't been freed, compensation¦56157 needs to be \add paid\add*.\f + \fr 19:20 \ft We as modern readers don't understand all the dynamics of this seemingly complex social situation.\f* They¦56160 mustn't be executed¦56160, because¦56135 she hadn't been freed.
\v 21 \add ≈However,\add* \add @that man\add* must¦56166 take a ram¦56176 to Yahweh¦56170 at the \add ≈sacred¦56174\add* tent's¦56174 entrance¦56173 for a guilt¦56177 offering¦56177,
\v 22 and the priest¦56181 will¦56179 make¦56179 \add ≈him¦56180 right with\add* Yahweh¦56185 by¦56182 means of that¦56189 guilt¦56183 offering¦56183 ram¦56182, and then¦56179 he'll¦56179 be¦56191 forgiven¦56191 for his¦56193 transgression.
\p
\v 23 When¦56198 you all enter into¦56201 the land¦56203 and plant¦56204 various kinds of fruit trees, you mustn't eat¦56220 the fruit for the first three¦56214 years¦56215—it should be \add regarded as\add* ‘uncircumcised¦56218’ \add for that duration\add*.
\v 24 Then¦56222 in¦56222 the¦56223 fourth¦56223 year¦56222, all that fruit¦56227 must¦56224 be \add regarded as\add* ‘sacred¦56228’—praise¦56229 offerings¦56229 for¦56230 Yahweh¦56230.
\v 25 \add ≈Finally,\add* in¦56232 the¦56233 fifth¦56233 year¦56232, you can eat¦56234 that fruit¦56237 and¦56232 add that produce¦56240 to¦56239 your harvest. I¦56241 am¦56242 your god¦56243 Yahweh¦56242.
\p
\v 26 Don't eat¦56246 anything with¦56247 the¦56249 blood¦56249 \add still in it\add*. Don't practice divination¦56251 or witchcraft.\x + \xo 19:26: a \xt Gen 9:4; Lev 7:26-27; 17:10-14; Deu 12:16,23; 15:23; \xo b \xt Deu 18:10.\x*
\v 27 Don't¦56259 \add have haircuts that\add* round¦56256 off¦56256 your hair at the sides, and¦56259 \add men\add*, don't¦56259 trim¦56260 the edges of your \add #beards¦56263\add*.\x + \xo 19:27-28: \xt Lev 21:5; Deu 14:1.\x*
\v 28 Don't¦56267 make cuts on your¦56269 bodies \add ≈when someone dies¦56266\add*, and¦56270 don't¦56267 \add ≈tattoo¦56270\add* yourselves¦56274. I¦56275 am¦56276 Yahweh¦56276.
\p
\v 29 don't¦56278 defile your¦56283 daughter¦56283 by¦56284 making¦56284 her¦56284 prostitute herself¦56284, \add ≈so the country\add* doesn't prostitute itself¦56287 and¦56289 become full¦56289 of wickedness¦56291.\x + \xo 19:29: \xt Deu 23:17.\x*
\v 30 Keep¦56296 my rest days, and¦56297 \add ≈respect\add* my sanctuary¦56297. I¦56299 am¦56300 Yahweh¦56300.\x + \xo 19:30: \xt Lev 26:2.\x*
\p
\v 31 Don't¦56302 turn¦56304 to mediums and¦56308 diviners—don't¦56302 make yourselves ‘unclean¦56314’ by means of them. I¦56316 am¦56317 your god¦56318 Yahweh¦56317.\x + \xo 19:31: \xt Deu 18:11; 1Sam 28:3; 2Ki 23:4; Isa 8:19.\x*
\p
\v 32 Stand up for those with grey¦56321 hair¦56321, and honour¦56323 the \add ≈presence\add* of¦56324 the elderly. \add ≈Honour¦56323 and respect\add* your¦56327 god¦56327. I¦56328 am¦56329 Yahweh¦56329.
\p
\v 33 ⇔Don't¦56338 \add ≈take advantage of¦56337\add* \add #foreigners\add* when they stay in your¦56337 land¦56337—\x + \xo 19:33-34: \xt Exo 22:21; Deu 24:17-18; 27:19.\x*
\v 34 you all must¦56344 treat \add #foreigners\add* the same as native-born¦56342 \add Israelis\add* and¦56350 love them like you \add ≡love\add* yourselves¦56352, because¦56353 you were¦56356 all foreigners in¦56357 Egypt¦56358 \add (Heb. Mitsrayim)\add*. I¦56359 am¦56360 your god¦56361 Yahweh¦56360.
\p
\v 35 Don't allow injustice¦56366 \add either\add* in \add ≈judging cases\add*, \add or by trading with rigged\add* weights¦56369 and¦56370 measures¦56368—\x + \xo 19:35-36: \xt Deu 25:13-16; Prv 20:10; Eze 45:10.\x*
\v 36 your scales and weights¦56374 and measuring containers must¦56381 be honest. I¦56383 am¦56384 your god¦56385 Yahweh¦56384 who¦56386 brought¦56388 you all out¦56388 of¦56390 Egypt¦56391 \add (Heb. Mitsrayim)\add*.
\v 37 You all¦56396 must¦56393 \add ≈obey my¦56398 instructions¦56398 and decisions¦56403\add* and \add ≈stick to\add* them¦56405. I¦56406 am¦56407 Yahweh¦56407.
\c 20
\s1 Penalties for disobedience
\rem /s1 Penalties for Violations of Holiness; Punishments for Sin; Penalties for Disobedience; Punishments for Disobedience
\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦56411 told¦56415 Mosheh¦56414:
\p
\v 2 Tell the \add ≈Israeli¦56419 people\add* that if any of them, or any foreigner staying in¦56432 Yisrael¦56420, gives¦56434 any of their \add ≈children\add* to¦56436 Molek¦56436, then¦56417 \add *that person\add* must \add ≈definitely be¦56438 executed¦56438\add*—the people must do it by throwing rocks¦56441 at them.
\v 3 \add Yes,\add* I myself will¦56445 \add ≈personally punish\add* that¦56450 person¦56449 and¦56444 cut¦56451 them off¦56451 from¦56453 the¦56453 people¦56454 for giving¦56457 their \add ≈child\add* to¦56458 Molek¦56458 and so¦56459 making¦56460 my sanctuary¦56463 ‘unclean¦56460’ and profaning¦56464 my sacred¦56468 name¦56467.
\v 4 If¦56470 the people¦56473 of¦56473 the land¦56474 \add just\add* hides their eyes¦56477 from¦56478 \add seeing\add* anyone¦56483 offering their \add ≈child\add* to Molek¦56484 so they¦56472 don't¦56485 have to execute \add @that person\add*,
\v 5 then¦56489 I'll \add also\add* remove that¦56495 \add other\add* person¦56494 and¦56489 their clan¦56496. I'll cut¦56497 them off¦56497 from¦56508 their people¦56509, along with anyone else who¦56503 practises prostitution¦56503 by¦56505 prostituting¦56505 themselves to Molek¦56507.
\p
\v 6 I'll \add ≈take action against\add* any person¦56511 who¦56512 turns¦56513 to mediums or diviners to prostitute¦56520 themselves to them, and¦56511 I'll cut¦56528 them off¦56528 from¦56530 their people¦56531.
\v 7 You¦56533 must¦56533 keep¦56533 yourselves¦56533 \add ≈separate from those kinds of¦56539 things to be¦56534\add* holy¦56535, because¦56536 I¦56537, Yahweh¦56538, am¦56538 your god¦56539.
\v 8 You all must¦56541 \add ≈follow my¦56544 instructions¦56544\add* and¦56545 \add ≈implement\add* them¦56546. I¦56547 am¦56548 Yahweh¦56548 who¦56549 \add ≈makes you different from other people groups\add*.
\p
\v 9 Any person who¦56555 curses¦56556 their father¦56559 or mother¦56562 must¦56556 be \add ≈executed¦56564\add*—their blood¦56568 will¦56564 be on¦56569 \add @their own head\add* for cursing their \add ≈parents¦56562\add*.\x + \xo 20:9: \xt Exo 21:17; Mat 15:4; Mrk 7:10.\x*
\p
\v 10 Any man who¦56572 commits¦56573 adultery¦56587 with another man's¦56577 wife, maybe even his¦56583 neighbours¦56583 wife, must¦56573 be¦56586 \add ≈executed¦56586\add*—both the \add ≈man and¦56571 the woman\add*.\x + \xo 20:10: \xt Exo 20:14; Lev 18:20; Deu 5:18.\x*
\v 11 Any man¦56590 who¦56591 sleeps with¦56593 any of his father's wives, has¦56599 exposed¦56599 his father's nakedness¦56597. Both¦56603 of them¦56603 must¦56592 be \add ≈executed¦56602\add*—their blood¦56604 is on¦56605 \add @their own heads\add*.\x + \xo 20:11: \xt Lev 18:8; Deu 22:30; 27:20.\x*
\v 12 If a man¦56607 sleeps with¦56610 his¦56612 daughter-in-law¦56612, both¦56615 of¦56615 them¦56615 must¦56609 be¦56614 executed¦56614. That's perversion and¦56607 so their blood¦56618 is on¦56619 \add @their own heads\add*.\x + \xo 20:12: \xt Lev 18:15.\x*
\v 13 If a man \add ≈has a sexual relationship\add* with¦56624 another man, both of them have¦56630 done¦56630 something detestable and¦56621 both of them must¦56623 be¦56633 executed¦56633—their blood¦56634 is on¦56635 \add @their own heads\add*.\x + \xo 20:13: \xt Lev 18:22.\x*
\v 14 If a man¦56637 takes both a mother¦56645 and¦56637 her¦56645 daughter as wives, then¦56637 that's wicked. They must¦56639 all be burnt¦56649 \add ≈to death\add* so that depravity won't¦56652 \add take root\add* among¦56656 you.
\p
\v 15 If a man \add tries to\add* \add ≈have sex with\add* an¦56662 animal, that man must be executed¦56664 and¦56658 the¦56667 animal must \add also\add* be killed¦56668.\x + \xo 20:15-16: \xt Exo 22:19; Lev 18:23; Deu 27:21.\x*
\v 16 If a woman \add ≈presents herself sexually\add* to¦56673 any¦56675 animal, you¦56680 must¦56672 \add ≈execute\add* the woman and¦56670 kill¦56680 the animal—their blood¦56689 is on¦56690 \add @their own heads\add*.
\p
\v 17 If a man¦56692 \add ?≈sleeps with\add* his sister¦56698 (whether on his father's¦56701 or¦56702 mother's¦56705 side) and they see each other's nakedness, it's¦56717 a disgrace and they must be¦56718 cut¦56718 off¦56718 from their¦56721 people¦56721—he's exposed¦56724 her¦56709 nakedness and he must bear¦56726 his wickedness.\x + \xo 20:17: \xt Lev 18:9; Deu 27:22.\x*
\v 18 If a man¦56728 \add ≈sleeps\add* with a woman¦56734 who's menstruating¦56735, he's exposed¦56745 her nakedness¦56739 and¦56728 uncovered¦56736 the \add ≈source\add* of her blood¦56749, \add so\add* they¦56750 must¦56731 both¦56751 be¦56750 cut¦56750 off¦56750 from¦56752 among their¦56753 people¦56753.\x + \xo 20:18: \xt Lev 18:19.\x*
\p
\v 19 You mustn't expose the nakedness¦56755 of your sister (whether on your father's¦56759 side or mother's¦56757 side) because¦56762 \add that's like\add* exposing your own \add ≈body\add*. They¦56768 must¦56759 bear¦56768 their¦56767 wickedness.\x + \xo 20:19-20: \xt Lev 18:12-14.\x*
\v 20 A man¦56770 who¦56771 \add ≈sleeps\add* with¦56773 his aunt¦56775, he's¦56778 exposed¦56778 his uncle's¦56777 nakedness¦56776. They'll bear¦56780 their¦56779 wickedness \add by\add* dying¦56782 childless¦56781.
\v 21 If a man¦56784 \add ?≈marries\add* his brother's¦56790 wife¦56789, it's¦56792 \add ≈indecent\add*. He's exposed¦56795 his nakedness¦56793 \add and\add* they'll¦56797 be¦56797 childless¦56796.\x + \xo 20:21: \xt Lev 18:16.\x*
\p
\v 22 You all must¦56799 \add ≈obey my¦56804 instructions¦56804 and decisions¦56809\add* and \add ≈stick to\add* them¦56811, and then¦56799 the¦56816 land¦56816 that I'm¦56818 about¦56819 to take you into, won't¦56812 vomit¦56814 you all out.
\v 23 Don't¦56825 follow the \add ≈customs\add* of the \add #peoples\add* that¦56829 I'll drive out ahead¦56833 of you all, because¦56834 they¦56840 do¦56840 all of \add @the above\add* things, and¦56841 I detest them¦56842
\v 24 and I've¦56844 told you all that you yourselves will¦56852 inherit their¦56850 land—I'll¦56852 give¦56852 it¦56852 to you \add ≈to take¦56854 possession¦56854 of¦56854\add*. It's¦56855 a land flowing¦56857 with milk¦56858 and honey¦56859. I am¦56861 your god¦56862 Yahweh¦56861 who¦56863 separates¦56865 you all from¦56867 the¦56869 \add other\add* people¦56869 \add groups\add*.
\v 25 You all must¦56871 \add ≈distinguish\add* between¦56872 ‘clean’ and ‘unclean’ animals and birds. Don't¦56882 make¦56884 yourselves detestable¦56884 \add to me\add* with any animal¦56888 or bird or crawling creature which¦56894 I've¦56896 distinguished for¦56897 you all as ‘unclean’.
\v 26 You all must¦56900 be ‘holy’ to me¦56901, because¦56903 I Yahweh¦56906 am¦56904 holy, and¦56907 I've¦56907 set you all apart from¦56909 the¦56911 other \add ≈people¦56911 groups\add* to be mine.
\p
\v 27 Any man¦56915 or woman¦56918 who's a medium or diviner must be¦56927 executed¦56927—the people¦56929 must do it by throwing rocks¦56929 at them.
\c 21
\s1 Stricter instructions for priests
\rem /s1 The Holiness of the Priests; Instructions for the Priests; Rules for Priests; The Holiness of Priests
\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦56936 told Mosheh¦56939:
\p Tell Aharon's¦56945 descendants the priests¦56943 that they must¦56946 not defile themselves among¦56952 the \add ≈Israelis\add*, by touching anything that's not living¦56948
\v 2 apart from the¦56958 body of a close¦56958 relative¦56957 like a \add ≈parent, child,\add* brother¦56964
\v 3 or \add ≈unmarried\add* sister¦56966—the priest can become ‘unclean¦56976’ by means of one of them.
\v 4 He¦56979 must¦56979 not make¦56979 himself¦56979 ‘unclean¦56979’ \add if it's the death of\add* \add ?≈a relative only by marriage\add*.
\v 5 They¦56986 must¦56986 not shave¦56993 their heads or trim the¦56990 edges of their beards¦56991 or cut¦56996 their bodies \add in grief\add*.\x + \xo 21:5: \xt Lev 19:27-28; Deu 14:1.\x*
\p
\v 6 \add @The priests\add* must stay separate for their God¦57001 and¦57002 they must not¦57002 \add ≈tarnish his reputation¦57004\add* because¦57006 they present¦57014 the gifts to Yahweh¦57010—their god's \add ≈food¦57011\add*
\v 7 They¦57022 mustn't \add ?≈marry\add* a woman¦57023 who was a prostitute¦57019 or who has defiled herself \add some other way\add* or who is divorced¦57024 from her¦57025 husband¦57025, because¦57028 they're separated for their god¦57032.
\v 8 You¦57034 must \add ≈treat\add* him¦57034 as \add ≈set apart\add* because he's¦57041 the¦57039 one presenting¦57042 your¦57040 god's \add ≈food\add*. He must be ‘holy’ for you, because I, Yahweh¦57050, am¦57048 holy and¦57034 I set you all apart as ‘holy’.
\v 9 If¦57056 a priest's¦57055 daughter¦57053 prostituted¦57058 herself¦57057, she would be profaning¦57057 her¦57061 father¦57061 \add so\add* must¦57057 be burnt¦57065 \add to death\add*.
\p
\v 10 The priest¦57068 who is chief of all his brothers¦57070 and who had the anointing¦57079 oil¦57078 poured¦57073 over his head¦57076, and \add ≈who has¦57080 the responsibility of\add* wearing the \add special\add* clothing, must not \add ≈wear¦57084 his hair loose\add*, and he¦57080 must not tear¦57095 his clothes¦57087 \add in grief\add*.
\v 11 He¦57103 mustn't approach \em any\em* dead¦57101 body—not \add even\add* his \add own\add* \add ≈parents¦57105\add*—he¦57107 mustn't make¦57107 himself¦57107 ‘unclean¦57107’.
\v 12 \add Even for a death,\add* he mustn't leave \add his duties in\add* the sanctuary, and¦57109 he mustn't profane¦57115 the sanctuary of¦57117 his god¦57118, because¦57119 he's been consecrated¦57120 with the anointing¦57122 oil¦57121. I¦57125 am¦57126 Yahweh¦57126.
\v 13 He can \add only\add* \add ≈marry\add* a virgin¦57130—
\v 14 he¦57141 mustn't take¦57141 a widow¦57133 or a divorced¦57134 woman, or a defiled prostitute¦57136. He¦57147 can only \add ≈marry\add* an unmarried, \add ≈Israeli\add* girl,
\v 15 then¦57150 he¦57152 won't¦57150 profane¦57152 his offspring among¦57154 his relatives, because¦57155 I¦57156 am¦57157 Yahweh¦57157 who¦57158 sets¦57158 him¦57158 apart¦57158 as¦57158 ‘holy¦57158’.
\p
\v 16 Then Yahweh¦57162 told¦57166 Mosheh¦57165,
\p
\v 17 Tell Aharon¦57171 that \add ≈none of his descendants\add* who have a \add ≈deformity\add* should ever approach to present¦57182 the¦57183 food¦57183 for his god¦57184.
\v 18 \add ≈Yes,\add* no man who has a \add ≈deformity\add* must¦57195 approach \add to offer a sacrifice\add*, i.e., no one who's blind¦57197, lame¦57199, mutilated, or \add ≈with a swelling\add*,
\v 19 or with a broken foot¦57212 or hand¦57215,
\v 20 or a hunchback¦57219 or dwarf, or with an eye¦57225 defect¦57224, with a scab or rash¦57227, or anyone with a crushed¦57231 testicle¦57232.
\v 21 Any \add ≈descendant of\add* Aharon¦57242 the priest¦57243 with a blemish¦57240 mustn't approach to preset a gift to Yahweh¦57250—no that person mustn't approach to present¦57246 god's food.
\v 22 However, they can eat¦57267 those gifts for God¦57261, including¦57264 the sacred and¦57264 very sacred \add ≈portions\add*.
\v 23 \add ≈Despite that,\add* they mustn't enter past the curtain¦57272 or approach the altar¦57277 if¦57280 they have a defect on¦57283 \add ≈their¦57292 body\add*. They mustn't profane¦57285 my¦57288 sanctuary¦57288 because¦57280 I¦57290 am¦57291 Yahweh¦57291 who¦57292 sets¦57292 them¦57292 apart¦57292 as¦57292 ‘holy¦57292’.
\p
\v 24 \add ≈So¦57294\add* Mosheh¦57295 told \add all\add* that to¦57296 Aharon¦57298 and his¦57301 sons¦57301, and all the¦57306 \add ≈Israelis¦57306\add*.
\c 22
\s1 Offerings to Yahweh become sacred
\rem /s1 The Use of Holy Offerings; The Holiness of the Offerings
\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦57311 told¦57315 Mosheh¦57314:
\p
\v 2 Tell¦57328 Aharon¦57320 and his¦57323 sons¦57323 that¦57335 they must¦57330 \add ≈carefully honour\add* the holy things¦57325 \add offered\add* by the \add ≈Israeli¦57326\add* people¦57326, and they mustn't profane¦57330 my holy \add ≈reputation¦57333\add*. I¦57339 am¦57340 Yahweh¦57340.
\v 3 Tell them that \add ≈throughout\add* the generations¦57344, any \add ≈of your descendants\add* who¦57349 is ‘unclean¦57364’ and approaches things¦57357 that have become holy because the people¦57360 have consecrated them to¦57363 Yahweh, \add @that person\add* will¦57366 be¦57366 cut¦57366 off¦57366 from¦57369 me¦57369. I¦57370 am¦57371 Yahweh.
\p
\v 4 Any man who's a descendant of Aharon¦57376, if he has a skin¦57378 disease¦57378 or¦57379 a discharge¦57380, he mustn't eat¦57383 any of the sacred \add >food\add* until¦57384 he's ‘clean’ \add again\add*. \add ≈The¦57387 same applies if\add* he's touched¦57387 any ‘unclean¦57390’ corpse¦57392, anyone¦57394 who's had a seminal emission,
\v 5 anyone¦57405 who's¦57406 touched¦57407 any swarming¦57410 \add >creature\add* that makes him ‘unclean’ or¦57415 touches \add another\add* person who makes him ‘unclean’ (whatever that person's uncleanness¦57422 is).
\v 6 \add No,\add* the man who's¦57425 touched¦57426 any of those will be¦57429 ‘unclean¦57429’ until the evening¦57432 and¦57433 he mustn't eat¦57434 any of the sacred¦57437 \add >food\add* until he's¦57441 washed¦57441 his¦57442 body¦57442 with¦57443 water¦57443.
\v 7 When¦57445 the¦57446 sun¦57446 sets, then¦57445 he'll¦57447 be ‘clean¦57447’ and¦57445 will be able to eat¦57449 any¦57450 of those sacred¦57452 \add >offerings\add* because¦57453 that's his¦57454 food¦57454.
\v 8 \add ≈But¦57458\add* he¦57460 must¦57460 \add ≈never\add* eat¦57460 \add ≈an animal¦57458 found dead\add* or torn¦57458 \add by wild animals\add* and¦57458 become¦57461 ‘unclean¦57461’ \add ≈in that way\add*. I¦57464 am¦57465 Yahweh¦57465.
\p
\v 9 \add @The priests\add* must¦57467 \add ≈follow my¦57470 instructions\add* so they won't¦57471 have to bear¦57473 their¦57482 own disobedience and¦57467 die¦57476 from it because¦57478 they profaned¦57479 them. I¦57480 am¦57481 Yahweh¦57481 who¦57482 makes them sacred¦57482.
\p
\v 10 \add ≈However,\add* no stranger¦57486 may eat the sacred¦57490 \add >food\add*, \add e.g.,\add* someone staying with the priest¦57492, or his hired¦57493 servant.
\v 11 If the priest had purchased \add ≈the person\add* with \add ≈cash¦57505\add*, then¦57499 \add @that person\add* can eat¦57507 it¦57508, plus¦57509 anyone¦57509 that was born¦57509 into \add @the priest's\add* \add ≈household¦57510\add*.
\v 12 A priest's¦57517 daughter¦57515 who \add ≈is married by\add* \add ≈someone who's not¦57525 a priest\add* can \add no longer\add* eat¦57526 those sacred¦57524 \add ≈offerings\add*.
\v 13 \add However, in the future\add* if she became a widow¦57533 or was divorced¦57534 without having had children, and¦57528 if she has returned¦57538 to¦57537 her father's¦57542 house¦57541 like when she was young, then¦57528 she can eat \add ≈the same food¦57544 as her father\add*, \add ≈but¦57528 no\add* stranger¦57549 may eat it¦57553.
\p
\v 14 If¦57557 someone¦57556 accidentally eats¦57559 something that's sacred¦57560, then they must¦57559 \add ≈pay back the full value plus¦57556 20%\add* to¦57566 the priest¦57566.
\p
\v 15 \add ≈So¦57571\add* \add in summary\add*, \add @the priests\add* must¦57572 not¦57571 profane¦57572 the sacred¦57575 things¦57575 \add contributed by\add* the \add ≈Israelis¦57576\add* and¦57571 which¦57579 they've \add ≈offered\add* to¦57582 Yahweh¦57582
\v 16 or else they'll¦57584 cause¦57584 themselves to bear¦57584 the guilt¦57587 from their¦57591 disobedience concerning eating¦57588 sacred \add >food\add*, because¦57592 I¦57593 am¦57594 Yahweh¦57594 who¦57595 has separated them¦57595 to be sacred.
\rem /s1 Worthy and Unworthy Offerings; Unacceptable Sacrifices; Acceptable Offerings
\p
\v 17 The Yahweh¦57599 told¦57603 Mosheh¦57602:
\p
\v 18 Tell Aharon¦57608 and his¦57611 sons¦57611, and all¦57613 the \add ≈Israelis¦57615\add* that¦57636 any \add ≈Israeli¦57615\add* or outsider \add ≈residing\add* in¦57626 Yisrael¦57616, when they¦57638 present their¦57632 burnt¦57640 offering to¦57633 Yahweh¦57639, whether it's for a vow or for a freewill¦57635 offering,
\v 19 to be accepted¦57642 it must¦57643 be a male¦57644 with no¦57643 defects¦57643, whether it's a cow, or a sheep, or a goat.
\v 20 Anything that¦57650 has a defect must¦57655 \em not\em* be presented¦57655 because¦57656 it wouldn't be acceptable¦57659 on your behalf.\x + \xo 22:20: \xt Deu 17:1.\x*
\v 21 \add ≈When¦57663 someone¦57663\add* presents¦57666 a sacrifice¦57667 of¦57667 peace¦57669 offerings¦57669 to Yahweh¦57670 to fulfill¦57671 a vow¦57673 or as a freewill¦57675 offering¦57675 from the herd¦57676 or the flock¦57678, to be accepted¦57681 it must¦57666 \add ≈flawless with no¦57679 defects¦57679\add*—
\v 22 not blind or with broken \add bones\add*, and not maimed or with an oozing sore¦57698 or rash¦57700 or scab. You all mustn't present¦57705 \add ≈anything like that\add* to Yahweh, and must¦57705 not \add even\add* offering¦57708 \add ≈any part of them¦57712\add* to Yahweh on¦57713 the¦57715 altar¦57715.
\v 23 \add ≈However,\add* if a cow¦57718 or a sheep¦57719 has something enlarged¦57720 or something stunted¦57721, it can be offered as a freewill¦57722 offering¦57722, but¦57718 it wouldn't be accepted¦57727 for a vow¦57725,
\v 24 and¦57729 you all must¦57734 never present¦57734 to¦57735 Yahweh¦57735 any animal that's bruised or torn¦57731 or cut¦57732.\f + \fr 22:24 \ft The Septuagint mentions ‘testicles’ here, which also correlates with 21:20.\f* You mustn't do¦57738 that in¦57736 your¦57736 \add ≈country\add*.
\p
\v 25 You all mustn't present¦57745 any of those¦57752 \add animals raised\add* by foreigners¦57743 to your god¦57749 because¦57753 they've been ruined and¦57740 are defective,\f + \fr 22:25 \ft Could this be related to the fact that they'd been neutered (as per v24 in the Septuagint)???\f* \add ≈so\add* they won't¦57744 be¦57759 accepted¦57759 for¦57760 you.
\p
\v 26 Then Yahweh¦57764 told¦57768 Mosheh¦57767:
\p
\v 27 A \add newborn\add* calf or lamb or goat¦57776 must¦57778 \add ≈remain with\add* its mother¦57783 for seven¦57780 days¦57781—it can be offered¦57789 as a sacrifice to Yahweh¦57790 from the eighth¦57785 day¦57784 onwards¦57786,
\v 28 \add ≈but¦57792\add* you mustn't slaughter a cow¦57792 or¦57793 a sheep¦57795 and¦57797 it's¦57796 \add ≈offspring\add* on \add ≈the same\add* day¦57802.
\v 29 When¦57805 you \add ≈offer\add* a thanksgiving¦57810 sacrifice to¦57811 Yahweh¦57811, it must¦57807 be \add ≈acceptable¦57812 as a sacrifice\add*
\v 30 and you can eat¦57817 it that¦57816 same day¦57815 \add but\add* \add ≈no part\add* of it should be¦57817 left¦57820 until¦57822 the morning¦57824. I¦57825 am¦57826 Yahweh¦57826.
\p
\v 31 You all must¦57828 \add ≈record my¦57829 instructions and¦57830 follow\add* them¦57831. I¦57832 am¦57833 Yahweh¦57833.
\v 32 You mustn't profane¦57836 the \add ≈reputation¦57839\add* of¦57839 my holiness, and¦57841 I will¦57841 demonstrate my holiness among the Israeli¦57843 people¦57843. I am¦57846 Yahweh¦57846 who¦57847 separates you all to be sacred¦57840—
