\v 21 You all must¦58179 proclaim¦58179 a sacred¦58186 assembly¦58184 that same day¦58182—you mustn't do¦58194 any \add ≈regular¦58195\add* work¦58191. That is a \add ≈permanent¦58196\add* rule that will continue \add ≈throughout\add* the generations¦58200 \add ≈no matter where you live\add*.
\p
\v 22 When¦58202 you all harvest your \add ≈crops\add*, don't \add ≈reap\add* to the very edge of your field¦58211 and don't \add ≈pick up stalks that drop on the ground\add*—they must¦58209 be left¦58219 for the poor and for foreigners \add without land\add*. I¦58221 am¦58222 your god¦58223, Yahweh¦58222.\x + \xo 23:22: \xt Lev 19:9-10; Deu 24:19-22.\x*
