\v 14 Take \add ≈that man\add* who cursed¦58764 outside¦58767 the camp¦58768, and \add ≈everyone¦58764 who heard¦58772 him\add* must place their¦58775 hands¦58775 on¦58776 his¦58778 head¦58778, and then \add ≈all¦58781 the people must execute him by throwing rocks¦58779 at\add* him.
\v 15 Then¦58785 tell the \add ≈people¦58787\add* that anyone who curses¦58795 God¦58796 must¦58789 bear¦58797 \add the results of\add* their own wickedness.
\v 16 Anyone¦58800 who¦58800 slanders¦58800 Yahweh's¦58803 \add ≈reputation¦58801\add* must be executed¦58805. The \add gathered assembly\add* must \add ≈throw rocks¦58806 at\add* them. \add It makes no difference\add* whether they're a \add ≈foreigner staying there\add*, or a native-born¦58814 \add Israeli\add*.
\p
\v 17 Anyone¦58820 who \add ≈murders\add* another person, must¦58822 \add ≈definitely be¦58828 executed¦58828\add*.\x + \xo 24:17: \xt Exo 21:12.\x*
