\v 2 Tell¦58929 the \add ≈Israelis¦58928\add* that when you all enter the land that I'm¦58938 giving¦58939 you, the land must¦58930 \add observe\add* a \add ≈rest year\add* for¦58944 Yahweh¦58944.
\v 3 ⇔You can \add ≈plant your crops\add*, prune¦58952 your \add ≈grapevines\add*, and \add ≈harvest\add* \add all\add* its¦58957 produce¦58957 for six¦58950 years¦58947,
\v 4 but¦58959 during the seventh¦58960 year¦58959, you must¦58963 \add ≈allow the land¦58964 to rest\add* \add to honour\add* Yahweh¦58966. You mustn't \add ≈plant any crops or prune¦58972 any grapevines\add*.
\v 5 Don't¦58977 \add systematically\add* harvest the self-sown¦58975 \add ≈crops\add* or the grapes¦58982 from the untrimmed¦58982 vines. It¦58987 must¦58978 be a rest year¦58985 for the land¦58988.
\v 6 \add ≈However, during\add* the rest year, the land¦58992 \add ≈will¦59000 provide\add* food¦58994 for you and your servants, and for your hired¦58998 workers and the foreigners who¦59000 are¦59000 living among you,
\v 7 as well as your¦59003 livestock¦59003 and¦59003 the \add wild\add* animals¦59004 across the land. Any produce¦59010 from the land can be¦59007 eaten¦59011.
\s1 The restoration celebration year
