\p
\v 3 If¦59811 you'll all \add ≈follow my instructions¦59813\add* and \add ≈remember my rules and obey\add* them¦59820,
\v 4 then¦59822 I'll¦59822 give¦59822 you all rain \add ≈in the proper season\add*, and the land¦59826 will produce crops and the trees in the countryside¦59829 will produce fruit¦59831.
\v 5 The \add grain\add* threshing¦59835 will \add ≈continue until\add* the grape harvest¦59838, and the grape harvesting¦59839 will \add ≈continue until\add* \add ≈it's time to plant new crops\add*, and so you'll all have \add ≈plenty of food¦59845\add* and you'll live securely¦59848 \add there\add* on your land¦59849.
\p
\v 6 Then¦59851 I'll give¦59851 peace¦59852 \add ≈in your country\add* \add ≈so that\add* you'll all sleep \add ≈without being afraid\add*. I'll \add ≈remove\add* the¦59853 wild¦59859 animals¦59858 from your \add ≈area\add* and¦59851 there'll¦59855 be no \add ≈raids or wars\add* in your \add ≈region¦59867\add*.
\v 7 You'll all \add be able to\add* chase away your enemies¦59872 and¦59873 \add ≈destroy them\add*—
\v 8 five¦59880 of you will chase away a hundred, and a hundred of you will chase away ten¦59884 thousand¦59884, and you'll \add ≈be able to¦59889 defeat\add* your enemies¦59887.
\p
\v 9 I'll \add ≈give you all my attention\add* and \add ≈bless¦59893 you with many¦59895 children\add*, and I'll \add ≈maintain\add* my agreement¦59900 with you all.
\v 10 You'll all \add still\add* \add ≈be eating¦59903 the previous year's grain\add* when the new harvest¦59908 \add ≈starts\add*, and¦59903 you'll have to \add ≈move\add* out¦59909 \add ≈that left-over grain\add* \add to make room for the new\add*.
\v 11 Then¦59911 I'll¦59911 put¦59911 my residence among¦59913 you all and¦59914 won't¦59914 \add ≈reject\add* you,
\v 12 and I'll¦59920 walk¦59920 among¦59921 you and be your god¦59924, and you'll all be my people¦59929.
\v 13 I am¦59932 your¦59944 god¦59933 Yahweh¦59932 who¦59934 brought¦59935 you all out¦59935 from being¦59939 slaves¦59941 in Egypt¦59938, and¦59942 I broke¦59942 the¦59943 \add ≈chains off you\add* \add ≈so that you all could walk¦59945 with heads erect\add*.
\s1 Punishments for disobedience
