\p
\v 14 \add ≈However,\add* if¦59950 you all won't listen¦59953 to¦59954 me¦59954 and¦59955 won't \add ≈follow all those¦59961 instructions\add*,\x + \xo 26:14-33: \xt Deu 28:15-68.\x*
\v 15 and if¦59963 you¦59980 all reject¦59966 my regulations¦59965 and my \add ≈values\add* \add ≈to the point of\add* hating my commands¦59979, thus breaking¦59980 my agreement¦59983,
\v 16 then this¦59990 is what I'll do¦59988 to you all: I'll \add ≈send\add* sudden¦59994 terror¦59994 to you all, and \add ≈wasting diseases and sicknesses\add*. You'll all \add ≈be wasting your time\add* sowing¦60005 seeds \add ≈because\add* your enemies¦60009 will eat¦60008 \add @the harvest\add*.
\v 17 I'll¦60011 \add ≈take action\add* against you, and you'll be defeated¦60014 by your enemies¦60016. You'll be ruled over¦60018 by those¦60019 who¦60019 hate¦60019 you, and you'll all \add ≈run away frightened\add* \add even\add* when no one's¦60023 chasing you.
\p
\v 18 If¦60027 you all \add still\add* won't¦60032 listen¦60033 to me¦60034 \add ≈after that\add*, then I'll¦60035 continue on to discipline¦60036 you seven¦60038 times over for your \add ≈disobedience\add*.
\v 19 Then¦60043 I'll \add ≈smash\add* your strong pride¦60046, and I'll make¦60048 the sky like iron¦60052 \add with no rain\add* and your land¦60055 \add hard\add* like bronze¦60056.
\v 20 Your \add ≈energy spent working\add* your land will¦60058 be¦60058 \add just\add* wasted \add ≈as\add* your land won't \add ≈produce its¦60067 crops\add*, and¦60058 the¦60069 trees won't \add ≈produce any fruit¦60072\add*.
\p
\v 21 Then¦60074 if¦60074 you're all \add still\add* \add ≈being contrary¦60078\add* and¦60074 unwilling to listen¦60081 to me¦60082, then¦60074 I'll¦60083 \add ≈send\add* seven¦60086 times more \add ≈deadly diseases\add* according¦60087 to your \add ≈disobedience\add*.
\v 22 Then¦60089 I'll¦60089 send¦60089 in the wild animals¦60093 \add ≈to\add* make¦60095 you childless¦60095 and to cut¦60097 back your livestocks¦60100, \add ≈thus diminishing¦60101 your numbers\add* and \add leaving\add* your roads¦60104 desolate¦60103.
\p
\v 23 Then¦60106 \add ≈after that\add* if¦60106 you¦60110 all \add still\add* \add ≈won't¦60109 accept my discipline¦60110\add* and¦60112 \add ≈continue to¦60111 oppose\add* me,
\v 24 then¦60116 I myself will \add ≈oppose\add* you all and¦60122 \add ≈punish\add* you all seven¦60127 times over for your \add ≈disobedience\add*.
\v 25 I'll \add ≈send armies against\add* you all to avenge¦60135 \add ≈the breaking of¦60142 our agreement¦60138\add*. You'll be \add ≈shut into\add* your cities¦60142 \add ≈where\add* I'll send diseases in¦60147 for you all, and¦60132 \add ≈allow your enemies to defeat\add* you.
\v 26 When I \add ≈limit your food¦60155 supplies\add*, ten¦60157 women¦60158 will bake¦60156 bread¦60159 in¦60160 one¦60161 oven¦60160 and¦60162 \add ≈it will be rationed\add* by¦60164 weight¦60164—you'll all eat¦60165 \add ≈but¦60156 never\add* be satisfied¦60167.
\p
\v 27 In spite of \add all\add* that¦60172, if you all \add still\add* won't¦60173 listen¦60174 to me, and¦60176 \add ≈continue to oppose\add* me,
\v 28 then¦60180 I'll \add ≈be in¦60182 a hostile rage against\add* you all and¦60185 I'll discipline¦60185 you seven¦60190 times \add more\add* for your \add ≈disobedience\add*
\v 29 and you'll \add start\add* eating your own sons¦60198 and daughters¦60200.
\v 30 I'll destroy¦60203 your \add ≈hilltop¦60206 shrines¦60206\add* and cut¦60207 down¦60207 you incense¦60210 altars¦60210, then¦60203 I'll \add ≈pile\add* your corpses on¦60215 top of¦60217 your idols' corpses, and I myself will¦60219 detest you all.
\v 31 I'll make¦60223 your cities¦60226 into \add ≈heaps of rubble\add* and I'll devastate¦60228 your sanctuaries¦60231 and \add no longer\add* smell¦60233 the¦60234 pleasing¦60235 aromas \add of your sacrifices\add*.
\p
\v 32 I'll¦60237 devastate¦60237 the¦60241 \add ≈region\add*, and¦60237 your enemies¦60244 who live in it¦60246 will be appalled¦60242.
\v 33 Then¦60248 I'll¦60249 scatter¦60249 you all among¦60250 \add other\add* nations¦60250 and then¦60248 \add ≈armies will come in\add* after¦60252 you and your land¦60255 will become desolate¦60256 and your cities¦60257 will become \add ≈rubble\add*,
\v 34 and the¦60263 land will enjoy all its rest \add ≈times\add* while it's desolate¦60269 and you're all in¦60271 your enemies' \add ≈countries\add*. The¦60275 land will \add ≈stop producing\add* and \add ≈enjoy its times of resting\add*.
\v 35 It¦60285 will¦60285 rest all through its desolation¦60284 since it didn't¦60288 get its rest times when¦60292 you lived on¦60293 it.
\p
\v 36 Then¦60295 those¦60295 of you who are left in your enemies' countries, I'll¦60297 make \add ≈you paranoid\add* \add there\add*—even the¦60300 sound¦60304 of a blowing leaf¦60305 will¦60302 make them run away as if someone's chasing them with a sword¦60310, and¦60295 they'll¦60307 fall¦60311 down even when no one's¦60313 chasing them.
\v 37 They'll stumble¦60315 over each other as¦60319 if \add ≈being attacked\add*, but¦60315 there¦60323 won't be¦60323 anyone¦60322 chasing them, and¦60315 then¦60315 you all won't have the energy to stand¦60328 up against your enemies¦60330.
\v 38 You'll die in \add various\add* countries¦60333 and¦60332 your enemies¦60337 will consume¦60334 you.
\v 39 Those¦60339 of you who¦60339 are left will¦60341 rot¦60341 away¦60341 amongst¦60340 the wickedness in your enemies' countries and¦60339 because of the wickedness of their ancestors¦60347.
\p
\v 40 \add ≈However,\add* if they confess¦60351 their wickedness and their ancestors' wickedness, that¦60360 they've disobeyed and neglected me, and \add ≈been hostile towards\add* me,
\v 41 (and that I¦60373 became hostile toward them and took their into their enemies' countries,) and humble¦60384 their \add ≈undisciplined\add* hearts¦60385 and \add ≈admit their disobedience\add*,
\v 42 then¦60393 I'll remember my¦60396 agreements with Yakov¦60397 \add !(Jacob¦60397)\add* and with Yitshak¦60402 \add !(Isaac¦60402)\add* and with Avraham¦60407, and I'll remember \add &this\add* land.
\v 43 The¦60412 land \add here\add* will have been deserted¦60419 by them¦60414 and will have enjoyed its¦60418 \add ≈times of¦60418 rest\add*, and they'll¦60422 accept¦60422 their¦60425 wickedness because¦60426 they rejected¦60429 my \add ≈values\add* and they \add ≈really\add* detested my regulations¦60432.
\v 44 \add ≈Despite that¦60440\add*, I won't reject¦60446 them in their enemies' countries, and I won't detest them enough to completely destroy them \add and\add* to break¦60451 my¦60452 agreement¦60452 with¦60453 them, because¦60454 I am¦60456 their god¦60457 Yahweh¦60456.
\v 45 I'll¦60459 remember¦60459 the \add ≈earlier\add* agreement¦60461 with their ancestors that I brought¦60464 out¦60464 of Egypt¦60468 while all the nations¦60470 watched me be their god¦60473. I am¦60475 Yahweh¦60475.
\p
\v 46 \add ≈The¦60487 above\add* are¦60478 the \add ≈instructions¦60478 and values and rules\add* that¦60481 Yahweh¦60483 \add ≈instilled\add* between¦60484 him and the \add ≈Israelis¦60486\add* through Mosheh¦60492 \add !(Moses¦60492)\add* there at Mt¦60488. Sinai¦60489.
