\v 9 If¦60637 it's an¦60627 animal that they're \add ≈promising\add* as a gift for Yahweh¦60632, then \add ?≈that animal becomes sacred¦60640\add*—
\v 10 it can't¦60644 be \add ≈exchanged¦60646 for¦60649 a different one (either better or¦60650 worse)\add*, \add ≈but¦60644\add* if¦60654 it does get substituted¦60663, then \add ≈both animals will¦60664 become sacred¦60666\add*.
\v 11 Any¦60669 ‘unclean¦60672’ animal cannot be presented to Yahweh¦60679, \add so if that's what was promised\add*, \add @the person\add* must¦60676 take the animal to the priest¦60685,
\v 12 and¦60692 a priest must¦60687 \add ≈give a fair valuation¦60694 according¦60694 to¦60694 the quality of¦60694 the animal\add*—the priest's¦60695 \add ≈decision¦60687 will¦60697 be¦60697 final\add*.
\v 13 \add ≈However,\add* if¦60699 it's¦60702 later bought back, then¦60699 an extra twenty¦60704 percent¦60703 must¦60702 be added to¦60705 that valuation¦60707.
